"[{\"key\":\"abilities-adaptability\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Adaptability\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Increases the same-type attack bonus from the usual 50% boost in power to 100%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-aftermath\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Aftermath\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes damage to an attacker equal to 1/4 of its max HP if the attacker knocks the Pokémon out using a move that makes direct contact.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-analytic\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Analytic\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's moves by 30% if the Pokémon goes last during a turn.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-anticipation\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Anticipation\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a warning if an opposing"
" Pokémon has supereffective moves or one-hit knockout moves. This warning occurs when the Pokémon with this Ability enters the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-arena-trap\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Arena Trap\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Prevents opposing Pokémon from fleeing or being switched out. Has no effect against Flying- or Ghost-type Pokémon and Pokémon with the Levitate Ability. Pokémon with the Run Away Ability can flee from a Pokémon with Arena Trap, but they will be prevented from switching out.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-aroma-veil\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Aroma Veil\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon's side of the battlefield from the effects of Disable, Encore, Taunt, and Torment. Also protects fro"
"m infatuation and the effect of the Cursed Body Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-ball-fetch\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Ball Fetch\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to retrieve a Poké Ball that was used in a battle but failed to catch a wild Pokémon. This effect will only apply to the first Poké Ball used. If the Pokémon is already holding an item, nothing happens.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-battery\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Battery\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of special moves used by the Pokémon's allies by 30%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-battle-armor\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Battle Armor\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Prevents opponents' damage-dealing moves from ever delivering a critical hit to the Pokémon"
".\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-berserk\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Berserk\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 1 stage when the Pokémon takes a hit that causes its HP to drop to 1/2 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-big-pecks\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Big Pecks\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from having its Defense lowered by the moves or Abilities of other Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-blaze\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Blaze\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's Fire-type moves by 50% when the Pokémon's HP drops to 1/3 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-bulletproof\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"titl"
"e\":\"Bulletproof\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from Acid Spray, Aura Sphere, Bullet Seed, Electro Ball, Energy Ball, Focus Blast, Gyro Ball, Octazooka, Pollen Puff, Pyro Ball, Rock Blast, Rock Wrecker, Seed Bomb, Shadow Ball, Sludge Bomb, Weather Ball, and Zap Cannon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-cheek-pouch\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Cheek Pouch\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Restores 1/3 of the Pokémon's max HP when the Pokémon eats a Berry (in addition to the Berry's usual benefits).\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-chlorophyll\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Chlorophyll\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the Pokémon's Speed in the harsh sunlight weather condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-clear-body\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Clear "
"Body\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from having its stats lowered by the moves or Abilities of other Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-cloud-nine\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Cloud Nine\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Negates the effects of weather conditions for all Pokémon on the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-competitive\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Competitive\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 2 stages whenever any of the Pokémon's stats are lowered due to an opponent's move or Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-compound-eyes\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Compound Eyes\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's accuracy by 30%.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely that the wi"
"ld Pokémon you encounter will be holding items if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-contrary\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Contrary\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Inverts the Pokémon's stat changes to have the opposite effect (lowered stats are instead raised and vice versa).\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-corrosion\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Corrosion\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to inflict the poisoned or badly poisoned status condition on Poison types and Steel types.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-cotton-down\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Cotton Down\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Scatters cotton fluff around the Pokémon when the Pokémon is hit by a damage-dealing move. This lowers the Speed of all other Pokémon on the battlefield.\\nEffects"
" outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-cursed-body\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Cursed Body\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 30% chance of disabling damage-dealing moves used against the Pokémon. Moves disabled this way cannot be used for 4 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-cute-charm\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Cute Charm\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 30% chance of inflicting infatuation on an attacker if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact. Gender-unknown Pokémon and Pokémon of the same gender are immune to this effect.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Pokémon of the opposite gender if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-damp\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Damp\",\"body\":\"Effects in ba"
"ttle: Prevents all Pokémon on the battlefield from using Explosion or Self-Destruct and nullifies the Aftermath Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-dauntless-shield\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Dauntless Shield\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Defense by 1 stage when the Pokémon enters the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-defiant\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Defiant\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Attack by 2 stages whenever any of the Pokémon's stats are lowered due to an opponent's move or Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-disguise\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Disguise\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from most damage the first time it is hit by a damage-dealing move. Then the Pokémon cha"
"nges to its Busted Form.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-drizzle\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Drizzle\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Triggers the rain weather condition when the Pokémon enters the battlefield. This weather condition lasts for 5 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-drought\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Drought\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Triggers the harsh sunlight weather condition when the Pokémon enters the battlefield. This weather condition lasts for 5 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-dry-skin\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Dry Skin\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Absorbs Water-type moves, making the Pokémon immune to their damage and effects. Instead, such moves restore 1/4 of the Pokémon's max HP. Restores 1/8 of the Pokémon's max HP at the "
"end of each turn in the rain weather condition. However, this Ability also increases the damage the Pokémon takes from Fire-type moves by 25% and reduces its HP by 1/8 of its maximum at the end of each turn in the harsh sunlight weather condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-early-bird\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Early Bird\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to wake more quickly when afflicted with the asleep status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-effect-spore\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Effect Spore\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 30% chance of inflicting the poisoned, paralysis, or asleep status condition on an attacker if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact. Grass-type Pokémon are immune to this effect.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield"
" guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-electric-surge\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Electric Surge\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Triggers Electric Terrain when the Pokémon enters the battlefield. This terrain lasts for 5 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-emergency-exit\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Emergency Exit\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to automatically switch out of battle when its HP drops to 1/2 or less during a Trainer battle. During a battle with a wild Pokémon, the Pokémon flees when its HP drops to 1/2 or less. This Ability still triggers for Dynamax Pokémon but uses their Dynamax HP as the starting number instead. Does not trigger in Max Raid Battles.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-filter\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Filter\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Reduces the damage the Pokémon takes from supere"
"ffective moves by 25%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-flame-body\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Flame Body\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 30% chance of inflicting the burned status condition on an attacker if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact.\\nEffects outside of battle: Halves the time it takes for Pokémon Eggs to hatch if a Pokémon in your party has this Ability. This effect is not increased by also having other Pokémon with Flame Body or Steam Engine in your party.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-flare-boost\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Flare Boost\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's special moves by 50% when the Pokémon has the burned status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-flash-fire\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\""
":\"Flash Fire\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Absorbs Fire-type moves, making the Pokémon immune to their damage and effects. Also boosts the power of the Pokémon's Fire-type moves by 50% the first time this is triggered in battle.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Fire-type Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-flower-gift\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Flower Gift\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's and the Pokémon's allies' Attack and Sp. Def by 50% each in the harsh sunlight weather condition. Causes Cherrim to change to its Sunshine Form in the harsh sunlight weather condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-fluffy\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Fluffy\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Halves the damage the Pokémon takes from moves that make direct contact. Doubles the damage the Pok"
"émon takes from Fire-type moves.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-forewarn\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Forewarn\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Reveals a move an opponent knows when the Pokémon with this Ability enters the battlefield. Damage-dealing moves with high power are prioritized.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-friend-guard\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Friend Guard\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Reduces the damage taken by the Pokémon's allies by 25%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-frisk\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Frisk\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Identifies opponents' held items when the Pokémon with this Ability enters the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-gluttony\",\"catego"
"ry\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Gluttony\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Held Berries that are normally eaten at very low HP will instead be eaten when the Pokémon's HP drops to 1/2 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-gooey\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Gooey\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Lowers the Speed of an attacker by 1 stage if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-gorilla-tactics\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Gorilla Tactics\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Attack by 1 stage, but the Pokémon can only use the first move it chooses when it enters the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-gulp-missile\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Gulp Missile\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Po"
"kémon to gulp up prey and change forms when it uses Surf or Dive. If the Pokémon's HP is more than 1/2 of its maximum, the Pokémon will catch an Arrokuda. If the Pokémon's HP is 1/2 of its maximum or below, the Pokémon will catch a Pikachu. When the Pokémon takes damage from an opponent, it will spit out its prey to damage the opponent and also trigger additional effects (Arrokuda: lowers opponent's Defense by 1 stage; Pikachu: inflicts paralysis status condition on the opponent).\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-guts\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Guts\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Attack by 50% when the Pokémon is affected by a status condition. Although the burned status condition would usually lower the Pokémon's Attack, the Guts Ability prevents this.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-harvest\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"titl"
"e\":\"Harvest\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 50% chance of restoring one of the Pokémon's used Berries at the end of each turn. This becomes guaranteed in the harsh sunlight weather condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Grass-type Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-healer\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Healer\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 30% chance that an ally Pokémon's status condition will be healed at the end of each turn.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-heatproof\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Heatproof\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Halves the damage the Pokémon takes from Fire-type moves and from the burned status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-heavy-metal\",\"category\":\"Abilities\""
",\"title\":\"Heavy Metal\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the Pokémon's weight.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-honey-gather\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Honey Gather\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Has no effect.\\nEffects outside of battle: If the Pokémon has no held item, it sometimes finds a jar of Honey after a battle (even if it didn't participate). The chance of finding Honey increases with the Pokémon's level.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-huge-power\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Huge Power\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the Pokémon's Attack.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-hunger-switch\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Hunger Switch\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to change form at the end of each turn, rotating between Full Belly Mode and Hangry Mode.\\nEffects outside o"
"f battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-hustle\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Hustle\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Attack by 50% but lowers the accuracy of the Pokémon's physical moves by 20%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-hydration\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Hydration\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Heals the Pokémon's status conditions at the end of each turn in the rain weather condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-hyper-cutter\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Hyper Cutter\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from having its Attack lowered by the moves or Abilities of other Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-ice-body\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Ice Body\",\"body\":\"Effects in "
"battle: Restores 1/16 of the Pokémon's max HP at the end of each turn in the hail weather condition. Hail does not damage a Pokémon with this Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-ice-face\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Ice Face\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from damage the first time the Pokémon is hit by a physical move. Then the Pokémon's form changes from Ice Face to Noice Face. Does not protect from special moves. The Pokémon can return to its Ice Face form if the weather condition becomes hail, if it's sent out into battle during hail, or when the battle ends, allowing this Ability to be triggered again.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-ice-scales\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Ice Scales\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Halves the damage the Pokémon takes from special moves.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\""
"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-illuminate\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Illuminate\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Has no effect.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-immunity\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Immunity\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from the poisoned and badly poisoned status conditions.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-imposter\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Imposter\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Transforms the Pokémon into a copy of the opponent it is directly facing when it enters the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-infiltrator\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Infiltrator\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pok"
"émon's moves to hit despite Mist, Safeguard, or Substitute. Also prevents damage from being reduced by Aurora Veil, Light Screen, or Reflect.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it less likely you will encounter wild Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-innards-out\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Innards Out\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes damage to an attacker if the Pokémon with this Ability is knocked out. The attacker's HP is reduced by the same amount of HP as the attacked Pokémon had left before it was knocked out.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-inner-focus\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Inner Focus\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from flinching and from the effects of the Intimidate Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-insomnia\","
"\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Insomnia\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from the asleep status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-intimidate\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Intimidate\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Lowers opponents' Attack by 1 stage when the Pokémon with this Ability enters the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-intrepid-sword\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Intrepid Sword\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Attack by 1 stage when the Pokémon enters the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-iron-barbs\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Iron Barbs\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes damage to an attacker equal to 1/8 of its max HP if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact.\\nEff"
"ects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-iron-fist\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Iron Fist\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's punching moves by 20%. This affects Bullet Punch, Drain Punch, Dynamic Punch, Fire Punch, Focus Punch, Hammer Arm, Ice Punch, Mach Punch, Mega Punch, Meteor Mash, Power-Up Punch, Shadow Punch, and Thunder Punch.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-justified\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Justified\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Attack by 1 stage when the Pokémon is hit by a damage-dealing Dark-type move.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-keen-eye\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Keen Eye\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from having its accuracy lowered by opponents' moves. Ignores the effects of opponent"
"s' evasiveness-raising moves as well.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-klutz\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Klutz\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: The Pokémon can't use held items in battle, even if it is given an item to hold.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-leaf-guard\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Leaf Guard\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from status conditions in the harsh sunlight weather condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-levitate\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Levitate\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Gives the Pokémon immunity to damage-dealing Ground-type moves, as well as the effects of Spikes, Sticky Web, Toxic Spikes, and terrains.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-light-m"
"etal\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Light Metal\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Halves the Pokémon's weight.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-lightning-rod\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Lightning Rod\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Draws all Electric-type moves to the Pokémon. Absorbs Electric-type moves, making the Pokémon immune to their damage and effects. Instead, such moves raise the Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 1 stage.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Electric-type Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-limber\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Limber\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from the paralysis status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-magic-bounce\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Magic Bounce\",\"body"
"\":\"Effects in battle: Reflects back moves that attempt to lower the Pokémon's stats or inflict status conditions, as well as the effects of moves like Stealth Rock or Taunt.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-magic-guard\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Magic Guard\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from any damage not directly dealt by a move. This nullifies the damage from Abilities, weather conditions, status conditions, items, and ongoing move effects (such as Bind or Spikes).\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-marvel-scale\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Marvel Scale\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Defense by 50% when the Pokémon has a status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-merciless\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Merciless\",\"body"
"\":\"Effects in battle: Guarantees that the Pokémon's moves will deliver critical hits as long as the target has the poisoned or badly poisoned status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-mimicry\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Mimicry\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Changes the Pokémon's type depending on the terrain. Electric Terrain: Changes to Electric type. Grassy Terrain: Changes to Grass type. Misty Terrain: Changes to Fairy type. Psychic Terrain: Changes to Psychic type. If the terrain returns to normal, the Pokémon also returns to its regular type.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-minus\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Minus\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 50% if an ally has either the Plus or Minus Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abiliti"
"es-mirror-armor\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Mirror Armor\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Reflects back any attempt to lower the Pokémon's stats. This does not prevent damage from moves, but additional effects from moves like Breaking Swipe, Mud-Slap, or Psychic are applied to the move's user instead.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-misty-surge\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Misty Surge\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Triggers Misty Terrain when the Pokémon enters the battlefield. This terrain lasts for 5 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-mold-breaker\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Mold Breaker\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Makes the Pokémon's moves ignore the effects of Abilities. For example, Earthquake will hit even Pokémon with the Levitate Ability. Does not nullify Abilities that have effects after a move lands.\\nEffects outside of batt"
"le: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-moody\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Moody\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises one stat by 2 stages and lowers another by 1 stage at the end of each turn. When selecting a stat to raise, this Ability will not select a stat that cannot be raised any higher. The same applies when selecting a stat to lower.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-moxie\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Moxie\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Attack by 1 stage when the Pokémon uses a move that knocks out another Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-mummy\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Mummy\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Changes an attacker's Ability if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact. That attacker's Ability becomes Mummy. Fails with certai"
"n Abilities, however.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-natural-cure\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Natural Cure\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Heals the Pokémon's status conditions when the Pokémon is switched out of battle.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-neutralizing-gas\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Neutralizing Gas\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Nullifies the Abilities of all other Pokémon on the battlefield and prevents them from being activated. Fails with certain Abilities, however.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-no-guard\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"No Guard\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Moves used by or against the Pokémon don't miss.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\""
":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-oblivious\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Oblivious\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from infatuation, as well as the effects of Taunt and the Intimidate Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-overcoat\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Overcoat\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from taking damage in the hail and sandstorm weather conditions. Also protects it from Cotton Spore, Magic Powder, Poison Powder, Rage Powder, Sleep Powder, Spore, and Stun Spore, as well as the Effect Spore Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-overgrow\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Overgrow\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's Grass-type moves by 50% when the Pokémon's HP drops to 1/3 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official"
" Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-own-tempo\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Own Tempo\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from confusion and from the effects of the Intimidate Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-pastel-veil\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Pastel Veil\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon's side of the battlefield from the poisoned and badly poisoned status conditions.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-perish-body\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Perish Body\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: If the Pokémon is hit by a move that makes direct contact, both the Pokémon and the attacker will faint after 3 turns unless switched out.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-pickpocket\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Pickpocket\",\"b"
"ody\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to steal an attacker's held item if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact. If the Pokémon is already holding an item, nothing happens.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-pickup\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Pickup\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to pick up a held item that an opposing Pokémon used in the same turn. If the Pokémon with this Ability is already holding an item, nothing happens.\\nEffects outside of battle: If the Pokémon has no held item, it sometimes picks one up after a battle (even if it didn't participate) it picks up different items depending on its level.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-pixilate\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Pixilate\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Changes the Pokémon's Normal-type moves to Fairy type and boosts their power by 20%. This effect also app"
"lies to Max Moves. (Max Strike will become the Fairy-type Max Move, Max Starfall.)\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-plus\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Plus\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 50% if an ally has either the Plus or Minus Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-poison-point\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Poison Point\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 30% chance of inflicting the poisoned status condition on an attacker if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-poison-touch\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Poison Touch\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 30% chance of inflicting the poisoned status condition on a target if the Pokémon with this Ability hits the ta"
"rget with a move that makes direct contact.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-power-spot\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Power Spot\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of moves used by the adjacent Pokémon by 30%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-prankster\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Prankster\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Gives higher priority to the Pokémon's status moves. A move affected by this Ability will fail if the target is a Dark-type Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-pressure\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Pressure\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: When the Pokémon is targeted by an opponent's move, this Ability causes that move to lose an extra point from its PP.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{"
"\"key\":\"abilities-propeller-tail\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Propeller Tail\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to ignore the effects of the Lightning Rod and Storm Drain Abilities, as well as the Ally Switch, Follow Me, and Rage Powder moves.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-psychic-surge\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Psychic Surge\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Triggers Psychic Terrain when the Pokémon enters the battlefield. This terrain lasts for 5 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-punk-rock\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Punk Rock\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's sound-based moves, such as Boomburst and Overdrive, by 30%. Also halves the damage the Pokémon takes from sound-based moves.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-qu"
"eenly-majesty\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Queenly Majesty\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Prevents opposing Pokémon from using damage-dealing moves that have high priority.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-quick-feet\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Quick Feet\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Speed by 50% when the Pokémon has a status condition. Although the paralysis status condition would usually lower the Pokémon's Speed, the Quick Feet Ability prevents this.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it less likely you will encounter wild Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-rain-dish\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Rain Dish\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Restores 1/16 of the Pokémon's max HP at the end of each turn in the rain weather condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 3"
"59–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-rattled\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Rattled\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Speed by 1 stage when the Pokémon is hit by a damage-dealing Bug-, Ghost-, or Dark-type move or the Intimidate Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-receiver\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Receiver\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Copies the Ability of a defeated ally over to the Pokémon, replacing Receiver with that Ability. Fails with certain Abilities, however.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-reckless\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Reckless\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of any of the Pokémon's moves by 20% if those moves cause recoil damage.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-regenerator\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Regenerator\",\""
"body\":\"Effects in battle: Restores 1/3 of the Pokémon's max HP when the Pokémon is switched out of battle.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-ripen\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Ripen\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the effect of Berries eaten by the Pokémon. Doubles healing effects, damage reduction, stat changes, friendship gains, and damage dealt to an opponent. Has no effect on Berries that heal status conditions.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-rivalry\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Rivalry\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's moves by 25% if they are used against a target of the same gender as the Pokémon. If a target is of the opposite gender, moves' power goes down by 25%. No effect when the target's gender is unknown.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\""
"key\":\"abilities-rks-system\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"RKS System\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to change its type according to the memory disc it is holding.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-rock-head\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Rock Head\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from recoil damage from moves like Double-Edge and Take Down.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-run-away\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Run Away\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to always escape from a battle with a wild Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sand-force\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sand Force\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's Ground-, Rock-, and Steel-type moves by 30% in the sandstorm weather conditi"
"on. Sandstorms do not damage a Pokémon with this Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sand-rush\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sand Rush\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the Pokémon's Speed in the sandstorm weather condition. Sandstorms do not damage a Pokémon with this Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sand-spit\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sand Spit\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Triggers the sandstorm weather condition when the Pokémon takes damage. This weather condition lasts for 5 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sand-stream\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sand Stream\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Triggers the sandstorm weather condition when the Pokémon enters the battlefield. This weather condition lasts for 5 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle:"
" —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sand-veil\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sand Veil\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Lowers the accuracy of moves used on the Pokémon by 20% in the sandstorm weather condition. Sandstorms do not damage a Pokémon with this Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sap-sipper\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sap Sipper\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Absorbs Grass-type moves, making the Pokémon immune to their damage and effects. Instead, such moves raise the Pokémon's Attack by 1 stage.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-schooling\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Schooling\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to change to its School Form if its level is 20 or greater. It changes back to its Solo Form when its HP drops to 1/4 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citati"
"on\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-scrappy\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Scrappy\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to hit Ghost-type Pokémon with Normal- and Fighting-type moves. Also protects the Pokémon from the effects of the Intimidate Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-screen-cleaner\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Screen Cleaner\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Nullifies the effects of Aurora Veil, Light Screen, and Reflect for both sides of the battlefield when the Pokémon enters the battlefield.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-serene-grace\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Serene Grace\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the chances of the Pokémon's moves inflicting additional effects.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-s"
"hadow-tag\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Shadow Tag\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Prevents opposing Pokémon from fleeing or switching out. This effect is canceled if an opposing Pokémon also has this Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-shed-skin\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Shed Skin\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 33% chance of healing the Pokémon's status conditions at the end of each turn.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sheer-force\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sheer Force\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's moves by 30% if they can have additional effects. However, the additional effects do not trigger.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-shell-armor\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Shell Armor\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Preven"
"ts opponents' damage-dealing moves from ever delivering a critical hit to the Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-shield-dust\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Shield Dust\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from the additional effects of moves. However, the Pokémon is still affected by additional effects generated by Max Moves.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-simple\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Simple\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles any stat changes affecting the Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-skill-link\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Skill Link\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Ensures that the Pokémon's multihit moves always hit the maximum number of times. (Moves that can hit 2–5 times always hit 5 times.)\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"c"
"itation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-slush-rush\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Slush Rush\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the Pokémon's Speed in the hail weather condition. Hail does not damage a Pokémon with this Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sniper\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sniper\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's critical hits. Power increases by 125% rather than the usual 50%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-snow-cloak\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Snow Cloak\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Lowers the accuracy of moves used on the Pokémon by 20% in the hail weather condition. Hail does not damage ■ Pokémon with this Ability.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-snow-warning\",\"category\":\"Abil"
"ities\",\"title\":\"Snow Warning\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Triggers the hail weather condition when the Pokémon enters the battlefield. This weather condition lasts for 5 turns.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-solar-power\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Solar Power\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 50% in the harsh sunlight weather condition. But the Pokémon also loses 1/8 of its max HP at the end of each turn as long as that weather condition continues.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-solid-rock\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Solid Rock\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Reduces the damage the Pokémon takes from supereffective moves by 25%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-soundproof\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Soundproof\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle:"
" Protects the Pokémon from sound-based moves, such as Clanging Scales and Parting Shot.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-speed-boost\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Speed Boost\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Speed by 1 stage at the end of each turn.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-stall\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Stall\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to move last each turn.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-stalwart\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Stalwart\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Allows the Pokémon to ignore the effects of the Lightning Rod and Storm Drain Abilities, as well as the Ally Switch, Follow Me, and Rage Powder moves.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-st"
"amina\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Stamina\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Defense by 1 stage every time the Pokémon takes damage from a move.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-stance-change\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Stance Change\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to change from its Shield Forme to its Blade Forme when using a damage-dealing move. The Pokémon changes back to Shield Forme if King's Shield is used.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-static\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Static\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 30% chance of inflicting the paralysis status condition on an attacker if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Electric-type Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"cit"
"ation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-steadfast\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Steadfast\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Speed by 1 stage every time the Pokémon flinches.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-steam-engine\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Steam Engine\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Raises the Pokémon's Speed to the max if the Pokémon is hit by a Fire- or Water-type move.\\nEffects outside of battle: Halves the time it takes for Pokémon Eggs to hatch if a Pokémon in your party has this Ability. This effect is not increased by also having other Pokémon with Flame Body or Steam Engine in your party.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-steelworker\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Steelworker\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's Steel-type moves by 50%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Officia"
"l Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-steely-spirit\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Steely Spirit\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of Steel-type moves for the Pokémon and its allies by 50%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-stench\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Stench\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Provides a 10% chance of making targets flinch when the Pokémon hits them with a damage-dealing move.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it less likely you will encounter wild Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sticky-hold\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sticky Hold\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Prevents the Pokémon's held item from being removed by other Pokémon's moves or Abilities.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-storm-drain\",\"category\":\"A"
"bilities\",\"title\":\"Storm Drain\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Draws all Water-type moves to the Pokémon. Absorbs Water-type moves, making the Pokémon immune to their damage and effects. Instead, such moves raise the Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 1 stage.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely you will encounter wild Water-type Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-strong-jaw\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Strong Jaw\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of Bite, Crunch, Fire Fang, Fishious Rend, Ice Fang, Jaw Lock, Poison Fang, Psychic Fangs, and Thunder Fang by 50%.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sturdy\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sturdy\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from one-hit knockout moves, like Horn Drill and Sheer Cold. If the Pokémon's HP is full, this Ability also leaves the Pokémon with 1 HP"
" if the Pokémon is hit by a move that would normally knock it out.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-suction-cups\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Suction Cups\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from being switched out by moves like Dragon Tail, Roar, and Whirlwind and items like Red Card.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-super-luck\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Super Luck\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Makes the Pokémon's moves more likely to deliver a critical hit.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it more likely that the wild Pokémon you encounter will be holding items if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-swarm\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Swarm\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's Bug-type moves by 50% when the Pokémon's HP dr"
"ops to 1/3 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-sweet-veil\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Sweet Veil\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon's side of the battlefield from the asleep status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-swift-swim\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Swift Swim\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the Pokémon's Speed in the rain weather condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-symbiosis\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Symbiosis\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to give its held item to an ally if that ally uses its own held item.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-synchronize\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Synchronize\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Sha"
"res the Pokémon's status conditions. If the Pokémon is inflicted with the poisoned, badly poisoned, paralysis, or burned status condition, the Pokémon that caused the status condition is also afflicted with it.\\nEffects outside of battle: Guarantees that the wild Pokémon you encounter will have the same Nature as your lead Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-tangled-feet\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Tangled Feet\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Lowers the accuracy of moves used on the Pokémon by 50% if the Pokémon with this Ability is confused.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-technician\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Technician\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's moves by 50% if their power is 60 or less. This effect is triggered for moves of variable power or moves affected by other factors as long as an"
" individual move's power ends up being 60 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-telepathy\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Telepathy\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Prevents the Pokémon from taking damage from allies.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-thick-fat\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Thick Fat\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Halves the damage the Pokémon takes from Fire- and Ice-type moves.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-tinted-lens\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Tinted Lens\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Makes the Pokémon's moves more effective against Pokémon that have a type advantage. (Half damage turns into regular damage, and 1/4 damage turns into half damage.)\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-t"
"orrent\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Torrent\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's Water-type moves by 50% when the Pokémon's HP drops to 1/3 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-tough-claws\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Tough Claws\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Boosts the power of the Pokémon's moves by 30% if those moves make direct contact.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-trace\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Trace\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Makes the Pokémon's Ability the same as the opponent's. Fails with certain Abilities, however. When the Pokémon is faced with multiple opponents, the Ability of one is chosen at random.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-truant\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Truant\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes t"
"he Pokémon to slack off, making its moves fail every other turn.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-unaware\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Unaware\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: When the Pokémon uses or is the target of a damage-dealing move, the move ignores changes to all opponents' stats except Speed.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-unburden\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Unburden\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Doubles the Pokémon's Speed if the Pokémon loses or consumes a held item. Its Speed returns to normal if the Pokémon gains a held item again. This Ability has no effect if the Pokémon starts the battle with no held item.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-unnerve\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Unnerve\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Prevents opposing Pokémon from eating Ber"
"ries they hold.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-vital-spirit\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Vital Spirit\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from the asleep status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-volt-absorb\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Volt Absorb\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Absorbs Electric-type moves, making the Pokémon immune to their damage and effects. Instead, such moves restore 1/4 of the Pokémon's max HP.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-wandering-spirit\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Wandering Spirit\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Exchanges the Pokémon's Ability with an attacker's if the attacker hits the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact. Fails with certain Abilities, however.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Offi"
"cial Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-water-absorb\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Water Absorb\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Absorbs Water-type moves, making the Pokémon immune to their damage and effects. Instead, such moves restore 1/4 of the Pokémon's max HP.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-water-bubble\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Water Bubble\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Halves the damage the Pokémon takes from Fire-type moves and protects the Pokémon from the burned status condition.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-water-veil\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Water Veil\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from the burned status condition.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-weak-armor\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Weak Armor\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Lowers the P"
"okémon's Defense by 1 stage when the Pokémon is hit by a physical move but also raises the Pokémon's Speed by 2 stages.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-white-smoke\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"White Smoke\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from having its stats lowered by the moves or Abilities of other Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: Makes it less likely you will encounter wild Pokémon if your lead Pokémon has this Ability.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-wimp-out\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Wimp Out\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to automatically switch out of battle when its HP drops to 1/2 or less during a Trainer battle. During a battle with a wild Pokémon, the Pokémon flees when its HP drops to 1/2 or less. This Ability still triggers for Dynamax Pokémon but uses their Dynamax HP as the starting number instead. Does not trig"
"ger in Max Raid Battles.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-wonder-guard\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Wonder Guard\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Protects the Pokémon from all moves except supereffective ones.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-wonder-skin\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Wonder Skin\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Makes status moves more likely to miss the Pokémon.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"abilities-zen-mode\",\"category\":\"Abilities\",\"title\":\"Zen Mode\",\"body\":\"Effects in battle: Causes the Pokémon to change to its Zen Mode form when its HP drops to 1/2 or less.\\nEffects outside of battle: —\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 359–364\"},{\"key\":\"appearance-salons-outfits-and-changing-rooms\",\"category\":\"Appearance\",\"title\":\"Salons, outfits and changing rooms\",\"bo"
"dy\":\"Salons in Motostoke, Hammerlocke, Circhester and Wyndon offer hair and makeup. Hair costs ¥3,000 and makeup ¥1,000; preview before confirming. Hairstyle, bangs, hair color, eyebrows, eyelashes, contact lenses and lip color depend on character style. Boutiques sell clothes; use their fitting rooms to change owned pieces. Gym uniforms are full outfits worn outside Gym missions; buying one does not replace the Gym Challenge mission uniform. The existing boutique and uniform panels list stock and saved ownership. Search Salon choices for every named option.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 313–334\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-abilities-and-held-items\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Abilities and held items\",\"body\":\"An Ability can alter damage, speed, weather, immunity, status, switching or rewards. Search Abilities for both battle and field effects. A Pokémon can have only one active Ability at once; a species may have multiple normal slots and a Hidden Ability. An "
"Ability Capsule switches compatible normal slots, not into a Hidden Ability in this base-game reference. Give one held item per Pokémon. Choice items restrict move selection while boosting a stat; Life Orb costs HP after damage; Focus Sash needs full HP and is consumed when triggered.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 174–177, 188–192\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-base-points-evs-and-training-items\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Base points, EVs and training items\",\"body\":\"Base points (EVs) come from defeating or catching Pokémon, vitamins, feathers and University jobs. Each stat caps at 252 and the six-stat total at 510. At level 100, four EVs correspond to one stat point before Nature; lower levels use the level-scaled stat calculation. Vitamins add 10 and feathers add 1 to their stat within the caps. Power items add points to a specific stat while reducing battle Speed; Macho Brace doubles EV gains. Pokérus can also multiply gains. Pomeg, Kelpsy, Qualot, Hondew, Gr"
"epa and Tamato Berries reduce HP, Attack, Defense, Sp. Atk, Sp. Def and Speed EVs respectively while raising friendship.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 178–180\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-dynamax-and-gigantamax\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Dynamax and Gigantamax\",\"body\":\"At Power Spots, an eligible Pokémon can Dynamax once per battle for three turns. Its current and maximum HP increase together; Dynamax Level raises that HP bonus. Damaging moves become type-based Max Moves; status moves become Max Guard. Gigantamax requires the appropriate factor and form, not just the species. A Gigantamax Pokémon’s signature type uses its G-Max Move instead of the ordinary Max Move. The Max moves and G-Max moves categories list all printed effects. Zacian, Zamazenta and Eternatus cannot Dynamax.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 192, 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-individual-strengths-judge-and-hyper-training\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Indivi"
"dual strengths, Judge and Hyper Training\",\"body\":\"Each stat has an individual strength (IV) from 0 to 31. Judge becomes available through Battle Tower progression and describes those values. Hyper Training at the Battle Tower requires level 100 and Bottle Caps: one regular cap trains one stat, while a Gold Bottle Cap trains all six. Hyper Training improves battle stats without changing the inherited IVs used for breeding. A Characteristic is only a clue to a high IV; it does not raise that stat.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 173–177\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-natures-flavors-and-mints\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Natures, flavors and Mints\",\"body\":\"A non-neutral Nature raises one stat by 10% and lowers another by 10%; HP is unaffected. The Natures category lists all 25 and their disliked flavors. Mints change the stat modifiers used for battle, while the Pokémon’s original Nature and breeding inheritance remain the same. Neutral Natures change neither stat. A"
" Berry that confuses a Pokémon because of flavor follows its actual Nature, not its Mint’s stat effect.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 173–180, 365\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-priority-speed-accuracy-and-critical-hits\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Priority, Speed, accuracy and critical hits\",\"body\":\"Priority brackets resolve before Speed; use Move priority for every printed exception. Tailwind boosts team Speed; Trick Room reverses Speed order within a priority bracket. Speed ties are random. Accuracy and evasiveness can change separately from the six main stats. A critical hit increases damage and can bypass unfavorable offensive or favorable defensive stat stages. High critical-hit moves, Focus Energy and certain Abilities or items change the rate. Protect can block many attacks, but repeated protection becomes less reliable and some moves bypass it.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–187, 352\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-single-double-and-raid-ba"
"ttles\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Single, Double and raid battles\",\"body\":\"Singles uses one active Pokémon per side; Doubles uses two. Each turn choose a move, switch, use an allowed item or attempt to flee in a wild battle. In Doubles, check a move’s target pattern before choosing it: some attacks hit both foes or allies as well. Max Raid Battles team four Pokémon against one Dynamax target, may use barriers and limit Dynamax to one ally at a time. Battle Tower battles use facility rules, selected teams and a level cap rather than ordinary route-battle rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 162–167\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-status-conditions-and-volatile-effects\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Status conditions and volatile effects\",\"body\":\"Burn chips HP and normally halves physical damage. Paralysis halves Speed and sometimes prevents an action; Electric types resist being paralyzed by the normal status rule. Poison chips HP; badly poisoned damage i"
"ncreases over successive turns. Sleep prevents ordinary actions until waking; freeze prevents action until thawing or a thawing move. A Pokémon can have only one major status at once. Confusion, infatuation, flinching, trapping and stat changes are separate effects and can coexist with a major status. Switching clears many temporary effects; it does not ordinarily cure a major condition.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 184–187\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-terrain-and-field-combinations\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Terrain and field combinations\",\"body\":\"Terrain normally affects grounded Pokémon. Electric Terrain boosts Electric attacks and prevents sleep; Grassy Terrain boosts Grass attacks, heals each turn and weakens Earthquake, Bulldoze and Magnitude; Psychic Terrain boosts Psychic attacks and blocks opponents’ priority moves against grounded targets; Misty Terrain prevents major status and reduces Dragon damage against grounded targets. A Terrain Extender len"
"gthens terrain. Combine Drizzle with Swift Swim, Drought with Chlorophyll, Trick Room with slow attackers, or Follow Me with a partner setting up. Check Ability immunity, target patterns and ally damage before using a combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 188–192\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-types-damage-and-team-coverage\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Types, damage and team coverage\",\"body\":\"Each Pokémon has one or two types; each move has one. Use the Type matchups category for all 18 attack types. Multiply the two defensive matchups for a dual-type target. A damaging move that matches either of its user’s types normally gets a 1.5× same-type attack bonus. Physical moves compare Attack with Defense; special moves compare Sp. Atk with Sp. Def. Status moves act through their effects rather than a base damage calculation. Build a team with useful defensive switches and several attack types; four similar attacks leave gaps.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield g"
"uide, pp. 168–172\"},{\"key\":\"battle-mechanics-weather-sun-rain-sandstorm-and-hail\",\"category\":\"Battle mechanics\",\"title\":\"Weather — sun, rain, sandstorm and hail\",\"body\":\"Sun boosts Fire damage and weakens Water; rain does the opposite. Sun lets Solar Beam and Solar Blade skip their charging turn; rain lets Thunder and Hurricane bypass their usual accuracy checks. Sandstorm damages non-Rock/Ground/Steel Pokémon and boosts Rock-type Sp. Def. Hail damages non-Ice Pokémon and makes Blizzard bypass its usual accuracy check. Relevant Abilities and items can prevent weather damage or extend weather duration. Weather set by an ordinary move or Ability lasts five turns, or eight with the appropriate weather rock; a later weather effect replaces it.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 188–191\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-abilities-that-attract-a-type\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Abilities that attract a type\",\"body\":\"Ability — Type it attracts\\nFlash Fire — Fire\\"
"nStorm Drain — Water\\nHarvest — Grass\\nLightning Rod, Static — Electric\\nMagnet Pull — Steel\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 177\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-battle-count-bonuses-for-brilliant-encounters\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Battle-count bonuses for Brilliant encounters\",\"body\":\"Number of times you battled a species — Effects on future encounters with that species\\nAt least one time — Becomes possible to encounter Brilliant Pokémon; + Chance of encountering Shiny Pokémon does not change\\nAt least 20 times — Around 1.3× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon; + Chance of encountering Shiny Pokémon does not change\\nAt least 50 times — Around 1.6× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon; + 2× the usual chance of encountering Shiny Pokémon\\nAt least 100 times — 2× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon; + 3× the usual chance of e"
"ncountering Shiny Pokémon\\nAt least 200 times — 2× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon; + 4× the usual chance of encountering Shiny Pokémon\\nAt least 400 times — 2× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon; + 5× the usual chance of encountering Shiny Pokémon\\nAt least 500 times — 2× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon; + 6× the usual chance of encountering Shiny Pokémon\\nUse the move, Ability and item entries for full effects and restrictions. Encounter bonuses describe the printed guide’s base-game rules; they do not predict the next encounter.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 176\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-confusion-curing-held-item-combination\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Confusion-curing held-item combination\",\"body\":\"Move; Thrash — Move; Outrage\\n+ Item; Persim Berry\\n= Confusion immediately cured\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Swo"
"rd/Shield guide, pp. 190\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-decorate-in-double-battles\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Decorate in Double Battles\",\"body\":\"Move\\nDecorate\\nBattle Format\\nDouble Battle\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 190\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-ev-reducing-berries\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"EV-reducing Berries\",\"body\":\"Pomeg Berry — Lowers a Pokémon's HP base points\\nKelpsy Berry — Lowers a Pokémon's Attack base points\\nQualot Berry — Lowers a Pokémon's Defense base points\\nHondew Berry — Lowers a Pokémon's Sp. Atk base points\\nGrepa Berry — Lowers a Pokémon's Sp. Def base points\\nTamato Berry — Lowers a Pokémon's Speed base points\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 179\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-experience-caps-by-badges\",\"category\""
":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Experience caps by badges\",\"body\":\"No Badges — Any opposing Pokémon over Lv. 25 will give Exp. Points as if they were a Lv. 25 Pokémon.\\n1 Badge — Any opposing Pokémon over Lv. 30 will give Exp. Points as if they were a Lv. 30 Pokémon.\\n2 Badges — Any opposing Pokémon over Lv. 35 will give Exp. Points as if they were a Lv. 35 Pokémon.\\n3 Badges — Any opposing Pokémon over Lv. 40 will give Exp. Points as if they were a Lv. 40 Pokémon.\\n4 Badges — Any opposing Pokémon over Lv. 45 will give Exp. Points as if they were a Lv. 45 Pokémon.\\n5 Badges — Any opposing Pokémon over Lv. 50 will give Exp. Points as if they were a Lv. 50 Pokémon.\\n6 Badges — Any opposing Pokémon over Lv. 55 will give Exp. Points as if they were a Lv. 55 Pokémon.\\n7 Badges — Any opposing Pokémon over Lv. 60 will give Exp. Points as if they were a Lv. 60 Pokémon.\\n8 Badges — No restrictions!\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation"
"\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 180\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-fishing-streak-bonuses\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Fishing streak bonuses\",\"body\":\"Number of successful hooks in a row — Effects on future fishing encounters\\n0–2 — Roughly the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon\\n3–6 — About 1.3× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon\\n7–14 — About 3.3× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon\\n15–24 — About 6.6× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon\\n25+ — About 16.6× the usual chance of encountering Brilliant Pokémon\\nUse the move, Ability and item entries for full effects and restrictions. Encounter bonuses describe the printed guide’s base-game rules; they do not predict the next encounter.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 177\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-magic-powder-and-type-changing-combinations\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Magic Powder and type-changing combinations\",\"bod"
"y\":\"Move — Move\\nMagic Powder — Night Slash\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 191\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-power-items-and-base-point-training\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Power items and base-point training\",\"body\":\"Power Weight — Increases HP base points every time you defeat or catch a Pokémon but reduces Speed while held\\nPower Bracer — Increases Attack base points every time you defeat or catch a Pokémon but reduces Speed while held\\nPower Belt — Increases Defense base points every time you defeat or catch a Pokémon but reduces Speed while held\\nPower Lens — Increases Sp. Atk base points every time you defeat or catch a Pokémon but reduces Speed while held\\nPower Band — Increases Sp. Def base points every time you defeat or catch a Pokémon but reduces Speed while held\\nPower Anklet — Increases Speed base points every time you defeat or catch a Pokémon but reduc"
"es Speed while held\\nMacho Brace — Doubles all base points earned from battles but reduces Speed while held\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 178\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-prankster-priority-combination\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Prankster priority combination\",\"body\":\"Ability; Prankster\\n+ Move; Status moves\\n= Moves get high priority in battle\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 189\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-raid-support-combination\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Raid support combination\",\"body\":\"Ability; Ice Scales — + — Move; Tailwind — + — Move; Helping Hand — = — Full support; in Max Raid; Battles\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 192\"},{\"key\":\"battle"
"-reference-tables-stat-stage-messages-and-modifiers\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Stat-stage messages and modifiers\",\"body\":\"Message you see in battle — What it means — Actual increase or decrease\\n[Pokémon's stat] rose! — Stat or variable was boosted by one stage — 50% increase for stats or about 30% for evasiveness or accuracy\\n[Pokémon's stat] rose sharply! — Stat or variable was boosted by two stages — 100% increase for stats or about 60% for evasiveness or accuracy\\n[Pokémon's stat] fell! — Stat or variable was reduced by one stage — About 30% decrease for stats or 25% for evasiveness or accuracy\\n[Pokémon's stat] harshly fell! — Stat or variable was reduced by two stages — 50% decrease for stats or 40% for evasiveness or accuracy\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 187\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-status-effects-and-specific-cures\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables"
"\",\"title\":\"Status, effects and specific cures\",\"body\":\"Status — Effect — Specific items for curing in battle\\nPOISONED — Deals damage each turn. If badly poisoned, the damage increases each turn. Lasts until cured. — Use an Antidote or a Pecha Berry\\nPARALYSIS — Halves Speed and causes moves to fail 25% of the time. Lasts until cured. — Use a Paralyze Heal or a Cheri Berry\\nASLEEP — Prevents usage of all moves except Sleep Talk and Snore. Lasts 1–3 turns. — Use an Awakening or a Chesto Berry\\nBURNED — Halves the power of the burned Pokémon's physical moves (p. 12). Deals damage each turn. Lasts until cured. — Use a Burn Heal or a Rawst Berry\\nFROZEN — Prevents usage of all moves except select, mostly Fire-type moves. Generally lasts several turns, but goes away if the Pokémon is hit with a Fire-type move or Scald. — Use an Ice Heal or an Aspear Berry\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 185\"},{\""
"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-steelworker-damage-combination\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Steelworker damage combination\",\"body\":\"Ability; Steelworker\\n+ Move; Steel-type moves\\n= Move power increased by 50%\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 189\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-terrain-setters-and-extending-items\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Terrain setters and extending items\",\"body\":\"Electric Terrain — Psychic Terrain — Grassy Terrain — Misty Terrain\\nMoves that cause it — Electric Terrain, Max Lightning — Psychic Terrain, Max Mindstorm — Grassy Terrain, Max Overgrowth — Misty Terrain, Max Starfall\\nAbility that causes it — Electric Surge — Psychic Surge — Grassy Surge — Misty Surge\\nEffects — • Boosts the power of Electric-type moves• Pokémon on the ground can't fall asleep — • Boosts the power of Psychic-type moves• Protects Pokémon on the ground from "
"priority moves — • Boosts the power of Grass-type moves• Restores a little HP to Pokémon on the ground each turn — • Halves the damage taken from Dragon-type moves• Protects Pokémon on the ground from status conditions and confusion\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 189\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-vitamins-and-target-stats\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Vitamins and target stats\",\"body\":\"HP Up — Adds base points to the HP of a single Pokémon when consumed\\nProtein — Adds base points to the Attack of a single Pokémon when consumed\\nIron — Adds base points to the Defense of a single Pokémon when consumed\\nCalcium — Adds base points to the Sp. Atk of a single Pokémon when consumed\\nZinc — Adds base points to the Sp. Def of a single Pokémon when consumed\\nCarbos — Adds base points to the Speed of a single Pokémon when consumed\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item descriptio"
"n before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 179\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-weather-ability-combinations\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Weather Ability combinations\",\"body\":\"Boosts Speed — Restores HP — Boosts power — Various bonuses\\nHarsh sunlight — Chlorophyll — — — Solar Power — Leaf Guard\\nRain — Swift Swim — Rain Dish, Dry Skin — — — Hydration\\nSandstorm — Sand Rush — — — Sand Force — Sand Veil\\nHail — Slush Rush — Ice Body — — — Snow Cloak\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 188\"},{\"key\":\"battle-reference-tables-weather-setters-and-extending-items\",\"category\":\"Battle reference tables\",\"title\":\"Weather setters and extending items\",\"body\":\"Harsh sunlight — Rain — Sandstorm — Hail\\nMoves that cause it — Sunny Day, Max Flare — Rain Dance, Max Geyser — Sandstorm, Max Rockfall — Hail, Max Hailstorm\\nAbility that causes it — Drought — D"
"rizzle — Sand Stream — Snow Warning\\nMajor effects — • Boosts the power of Fire-type moves• Lowers the power of Water-type moves• Lowers the accuracy of the moves Hurricane and Thunder• The HP-restoring moves Moonlight, Morning Sun, and Synthesis restore more HP• Prevents Pokémon from becoming frozen — • Boosts the power of Water-type moves• Lowers the power of Fire-type moves• The moves Hurricane and Thunder become 100% accurate• The HP-restoring moves Moonlight, Morning Sun, and Synthesis restore less HP — • Damages all non-Ground-, Rock-, or Steel-type Pokémon each turn• Boosts the Sp. Def of Rock-type Pokémon• The HP-restoring moves Moonlight, Morning Sun, and Synthesis restore less HP, and Shore Up restores more HP — • Damages all non-ice-type Pokémon each turn• The move Blizzard becomes 100% accurate• The HP-restoring moves Moonlight, Morning Sun, and Synthesis restore much less HP\\nCheck the full move, Ability or item description before applying the combination.\",\"citation\":\"Off"
