"re not inferred from OCR.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 292–293\"},{\"key\":\"camping-cooking-steps-and-quality\",\"category\":\"Camping\",\"title\":\"Cooking steps and quality\",\"body\":\"Choose an ingredient or plain curry, then up to ten Berries per camper. Ingredients determine the curry family; the combined Berry flavors determine spicy, dry, sweet, bitter, sour or neutral flavor. Fan to build a strong flame without burning, stir steadily without spilling, and add your heart when the circle reaches the green timing zone. Sparkles and Pokémon reactions indicate good cooking. Better ingredients, Berries and technique improve the class, but no single input guarantees Charizard Class. The five Curry quality entries list recovery effects. A recipe entry and a cooking-quality result are separate records.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 280–289\"},{\"key\":\"camping-friendship-tier-benefits\",\"category\":\"Camping\",\"title\":\"Friendship tier benefits\",\"body\":\"At the lowest tiers th"
"ere are no special battle bonuses. The camping-only higher tiers progressively add a chance to endure a hit at 1 HP, extra experience, recovery from status, avoidance of an attack, and more critical hits. The maximum tier has the broadest bonuses. A rater’s description and camp hearts describe friendship; they do not measure IVs, EVs, capture odds or a completed side quest. Bitter herbs restore health or status at the cost of friendship.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"camping-friendship-tiers-and-play\",\"category\":\"Camping\",\"title\":\"Friendship tiers and play\",\"body\":\"Use the Hammerlocke friendship rater and the hearts shown at camp to gauge your bond. Walking, level gains, play, curry and some Berries raise friendship; fainting and bitter herbal medicine can lower it. Ordinary activities stop short of the highest camping friendship tiers. At high friendship, story battles can grant survival, status recovery, experience, evasion and critical-hit benefits;"
" these bonuses are not a promise on every turn and are restricted in competitive facilities. Play with the feather toy or ball, call Pokémon over and let tired campers rest. Cooking may lead sociable Pokémon to give ingredients or eligible wild visitors to approach.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 280–289\"},{\"key\":\"camping-with-others-cooperative-cooking-and-communication\",\"category\":\"Camping with others\",\"title\":\"Cooperative cooking and communication\",\"body\":\"Up to four campers can cook together when the game’s communication features are available. Each contributes Berries, everyone fans and stirs, and each player times their heart addition. The host provides the ingredient. Other players’ Berries change the resulting flavor, so a strong-flavor contribution may help steer it without guaranteeing it. Joining a real player’s camp requires the corresponding local or online communication path, which the offline native runtime does not implement. NPC camps remain the offline "
"alternative.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 295–297\"},{\"key\":\"camping-with-others-npc-camps-on-routes-3-10\",\"category\":\"Camping with others\",\"title\":\"NPC camps on Routes 3–10\",\"body\":\"Every route from 3 through 10 has a resident camper’s tent. Interact with its owner to visit, play with the resident Pokémon and cook using the host’s ingredient plus your Berries. The route’s tent can become a Flying Taxi destination after visiting. These NPC camps work without networking. Search the route checklist for the local camp and directions. A curry made there still counts toward its corresponding Curry Dex recipe; the host, not the guest, chooses the main ingredient.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 295–297\"},{\"key\":\"card-backgrounds-ball-guy\",\"category\":\"Card backgrounds\",\"title\":\"Ball Guy\",\"body\":\"Background unlock group: Ball Guy. Unlock condition: After becoming Champion, speak to Ball Guy outside Motostoke Stadium.\\nVariants are individual choices within this un"
"lock group, not numbered native menu slots. Preview the art at Rotomi; this handbook does not reproduce the guide’s artwork.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 301–307\"},{\"key\":\"card-backgrounds-ballonlea-variant-1\",\"category\":\"Card backgrounds\",\"title\":\"Ballonlea — variant 1\",\"body\":\"Background unlock group: Ballonlea. Unlock condition: Arrive in Ballonlea through Glimwood Tangle.\\nVariants are individual choices within this unlock group, not numbered native menu slots. Preview the art at Rotomi; this handbook does not reproduce the guide’s artwork.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 301–307\"},{\"key\":\"card-backgrounds-ballonlea-variant-2\",\"category\":\"Card backgrounds\",\"title\":\"Ballonlea — variant 2\",\"body\":\"Background unlock group: Ballonlea. Unlock condition: Arrive in Ballonlea through Glimwood Tangle.\\nVariants are individual choices within this unlock group, not numbered native menu slots. Preview the art at Rotomi; this handbook does not reproduce the guide’"
