"\"body\":\"Rarity: Rare\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 279\"},{\"key\":\"friendship-tiers-1-not-friends\",\"category\":\"Friendship tiers\",\"title\":\"1 — Not friends\",\"body\":\"The rater suggests you may be too strict. No friendship battle bonus; avoid fainting and bitter herbs.\\nUse play and curry to develop the highest tiers; these are chances, not guaranteed outcomes.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"friendship-tiers-2-recently-met\",\"category\":\"Friendship tiers\",\"title\":\"2 — Recently met\",\"body\":\"The rater says it is still getting used to things. No friendship battle bonus.\\nUse play and curry to develop the highest tiers; these are chances, not guaranteed outcomes.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"friendship-tiers-3-average-bond\",\"category\":\"Friendship tiers\",\"title\":\"3 — Average bond\",\"body\":\"The rater says it likes you an average amount. No friendship battle bonus.\\nUse play and curry to develop the highest tiers; thes"
"e are chances, not guaranteed outcomes.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"friendship-tiers-4-becoming-good-friends\",\"category\":\"Friendship tiers\",\"title\":\"4 — Becoming good friends\",\"body\":\"One heart at camp. The rater says you are on your way to becoming good friends. No friendship battle bonus yet.\\nUse play and curry to develop the highest tiers; these are chances, not guaranteed outcomes.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"friendship-tiers-5-pretty-good-friends\",\"category\":\"Friendship tiers\",\"title\":\"5 — Pretty good friends\",\"body\":\"Two hearts at camp. The rater says you could become closer. No friendship battle bonus yet.\\nUse play and curry to develop the highest tiers; these are chances, not guaranteed outcomes.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"friendship-tiers-6-get-along-great\",\"category\":\"Friendship tiers\",\"title\":\"6 — Get along great\",\"body\":\"First camping-only tier. A small chance to s"
"urvive a hit that would normally knock out the Pokémon; it reacts on entering battle.\\nUse play and curry to develop the highest tiers; these are chances, not guaranteed outcomes.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"friendship-tiers-7-almost-best-friends\",\"category\":\"Friendship tiers\",\"title\":\"7 — Almost best friends\",\"body\":\"Higher camping-only tier. More survival chances, extra experience and a chance to recover from a status condition.\\nUse play and curry to develop the highest tiers; these are chances, not guaranteed outcomes.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"friendship-tiers-8-best-buddies\",\"category\":\"Friendship tiers\",\"title\":\"8 — Best buddies\",\"body\":\"Maximum camping tier. Survival, extra experience, status recovery, a chance to evade a move and a higher critical-hit ratio. Competitive facilities restrict these bonuses.\\nUse play and curry to develop the highest tiers; these are chances, not guaranteed outcomes.\",\"citat"
"ion\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 283–284\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-befuddle\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Befuddle\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Butterfree\\nType: Bug\\nEffect: Inflicts the poison, paralysis, or asleep status condition on all opposing Pokémon.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-centiferno\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Centiferno\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Centiskorch\\nType: Fire\\nEffect: Inflicts damage equal to 1/8 of max HP to all opponents at the end of each turn for 4–5 turns. Opponents cannot flee or be switched out of battle during that time.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-chi-strike\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Chi Strike\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Machamp\\nType: Fighting\\nEffect: Increases critical hit rates of all ally Pokémon by 2 stages.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-"
"g-max-cuddle\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Cuddle\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Eevee\\nType: Normal\\nEffect: Makes all opposing Pokémon become infatuated, which causes moves to fail 50% of the time.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-depletion\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Depletion\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Duraludon\\nType: Dragon\\nEffect: Reduces the PP of the moves used by all opposing Pokémon by 2.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-finale\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Finale\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Alcremie\\nType: Fairy\\nEffect: Restores 1/6 of all ally Pokémon's max HP.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-foam-burst\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Foam Burst\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Kingler\\nType: Water\\nEffect: Decreases the Speed stats of all opposing Pokémon by 2 stages.\",\"citation\":\""
"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-gold-rush\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Gold Rush\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Meowth\\nType: Normal\\nEffect: Pays out money after battle. The amount depends on the user's level and the number of times the move was used. First use: ₱100 × user's level. Second use: ₱300 × user's level. Third use: ₱600 × user's level. Also makes all opposing Pokémon confused.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-gravitas\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Gravitas\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Orbeetle\\nType: Psychic\\nEffect: Airborne Pokémon are grounded. Ground-type moves will now hit Pokémon normally immune to them. Prevents the use of Bounce, Fly, Flying Press, High Jump Kick, Magnet Rise, and Splash. Raises the accuracy of all Pokémon in battle. Lasts 5 turns.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-malodor\",\"category\":\"G-"
"Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Malodor\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Garbodor\\nType: Poison\\nEffect: Inflicts the poison status condition on all opposing Pokémon.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-resonance\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Resonance\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Lapras\\nType: Ice\\nEffect: Reduces damage from physical and special moves for 5 turns.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-sandblast\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Sandblast\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Sandaconda\\nType: Ground\\nEffect: Inflicts damage equal to 1/8 of max HP to all opponents at the end of each turn for 4–5 turns. Opponents cannot flee or be switched out of battle during that time.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-smite\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Smite\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Hatterene\\nType: Fairy\\nEffect: Makes all oppos"
"ing Pokémon confused.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-snooze\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Snooze\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Grimmsnarl\\nType: Dark\\nEffect: Inflicts the asleep status condition on the target at the end of the next turn unless the target switches out.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-steelsurge\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Steelsurge\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Copperajah\\nType: Steel\\nEffect: Damages Pokémon as they are sent out to the opposing side. This damage is Steel type and subject to type matchups.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-stonesurge\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Stonesurge\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Drednaw\\nType: Water\\nEffect: Damages Pokémon as they are sent out to the opposing side. This damage is Rock type and subject to type matchups.\",\"citation\":\"Official S"
"word/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-sweetness\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Sweetness\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Appletun\\nType: Grass\\nEffect: Heals the status conditions of all ally Pokémon in battle.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-tartness\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Tartness\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Flapple\\nType: Grass\\nEffect: Decreases the evasiveness of all opposing Pokémon by 1 stage.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-terror\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Terror\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Gengar\\nType: Ghost\\nEffect: Prevents all opposing Pokémon from fleeing or being switched out while this Pokémon is in battle.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-volcalith\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Volcalith\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Coalossal\\nType: Rock\\nEff"
"ect: Inflicts damage equal to 1/6 of max HP to all non-Rock-type opponents for 4 turns.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-volt-crash\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Volt Crash\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Pikachu\\nType: Electric\\nEffect: Inflicts the paralysis status condition on all opposing Pokémon.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-wildfire\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Wildfire\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Charizard\\nType: Fire\\nEffect: Inflicts damage equal to 1/6 of max HP to all non-Fire-type opponents for 4 turns.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"g-max-moves-g-max-wind-rage\",\"category\":\"G-Max moves\",\"title\":\"G-Max Wind Rage\",\"body\":\"User: Gigantamax Corviknight\\nType: Flying\\nEffect: Nullifies Aurora Veil, Light Screen, Mist, Reflect, and Safeguard on the opponents' side. Nullifies Spikes, Stealth Rock, Sticky Web, and Toxic"
" Spikes on both sides.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 216–229, 353\"},{\"key\":\"getting-started-catching-wild-pok-mon\",\"category\":\"Getting started\",\"title\":\"Catching wild Pokémon\",\"body\":\"Begin a wild battle, lower the target’s HP without knocking it out, and consider sleep or paralysis. Throw a ball from Bag or the battle’s ball shortcut. You cannot catch a Trainer’s Pokémon. Badge limits can block catching very strong wild Pokémon; return later after earning the required badge. Catching records the species in the Pokédex and awards experience. A Critical Capture is a special capture animation, not a guarantee that every attempt will succeed. Pokémon in rustling grass, visible wanderers, fishing spots and raid dens have different encounter rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 16–23\"},{\"key\":\"getting-started-controls-and-interaction\",\"category\":\"Getting started\",\"title\":\"Controls and interaction\",\"body\":\"Use the left stick to move and A to interact or confir"
"m. B cancels or returns. X opens the main menu. Full stick tilt runs; gentle tilt crouches in tall grass. Click the left stick to whistle or ring the bike bell. In the Wild Area, the right stick rotates the camera, its click changes zoom, and L resets the camera. + or − mounts or dismounts the Rotom Bike after you receive it. B, L or R uses the charged bike boost where allowed. Menu button prompts take precedence. Casual Controls can be enabled in Options for one-handed Joy-Con play, with limited camera control.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 2–9\"},{\"key\":\"getting-started-fishing-movement-and-fast-travel\",\"category\":\"Getting started\",\"title\":\"Fishing, movement and fast travel\",\"body\":\"At a bubbling water spot, face it and press A to cast; press A again when the bite prompt appears. The Rotom Bike begins on Route 5; its water upgrade comes on Route 9. Use the Town Map’s Flying Taxi for places you have already unlocked. Taxi access, route gates and water access are separat"
"e story unlocks. For the current route and return visits, use the area checklist and Route directions.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 22–30\"},{\"key\":\"getting-started-gym-badges-and-catching-limits\",\"category\":\"Getting started\",\"title\":\"Gym Badges and catching limits\",\"body\":\"Catching level caps by badge count: 0 → 20; 1 → 25; 2 → 30; 3 → 35; 4 → 40; 5 → 45; 6 → 50; 7 → 55; 8 → no catching level limit. Obedience rules for traded Pokémon differ from catch limits. Badges also unlock Mart stock, higher raid ranks and stronger training jobs. Read a row’s access note before treating a later visit as available.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 24–30\"},{\"key\":\"getting-started-main-menu-and-saving\",\"category\":\"Getting started\",\"title\":\"Main menu and saving\",\"body\":\"X opens the main menu. Pokémon manages your party and leads to summary, moves, held items and Boxes. Bag separates medicine, balls, battle items, Berries, held items, TMs, treasures and key items. Pokédex "
"records seen and caught species; Town Map selects destinations; League Card shows your card; Pokémon Camp starts camp on dry land; Mystery Gift and VS include communication features. Save from the menu before ending play. Autosave and other preferences are in Options. The native guide reads committed saves; browsing a chapter never writes into the game’s save.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 10–15\"},{\"key\":\"getting-started-party-boxes-and-healing\",\"category\":\"Getting started\",\"title\":\"Party, Boxes and healing\",\"body\":\"Carry up to six Pokémon; the top party slot normally enters a single battle first. Reorder from Pokémon. Open Boxes after the Box Link becomes available, except where the game restricts access. Check summaries for type, Ability, Nature, stats, moves and held items. Pokémon Centers restore HP, PP and status at no charge. Medicine can restore HP or remove conditions in the field; a fainted Pokémon needs a Revive or a Center. Give held items separately from usi"
"ng consumable medicine.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 10–21\"},{\"key\":\"hikers-exp-candy-l\",\"category\":\"Hikers\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy L\",\"body\":\"Rarity; (Up to 2 Badges): —\\nRarity; (2 to 8 Badges): —\\nRarity; (After becoming Champion): Rare\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 279\"},{\"key\":\"hikers-exp-candy-m\",\"category\":\"Hikers\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy M\",\"body\":\"Rarity; (Up to 2 Badges): —\\nRarity; (2 to 8 Badges): Rare\\nRarity; (After becoming Champion): Common\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 279\"},{\"key\":\"hikers-exp-candy-m-2\",\"category\":\"Hikers\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy M ×2\",\"body\":\"Rarity; (Up to 2 Badges): —\\nRarity; (2 to 8 Badges): —\\nRarity; (After becoming Champion): Uncommon\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 279\"},{\"key\":\"hikers-exp-candy-s\",\"category\":\"Hikers\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy S\",\"body\":\"Rarity; (Up to 2 Badges): Rare\\nRarity; (2 to 8 Badges): Common\\nRarity; (After becoming Champion): Common\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield gui"
