"\"items-ability-capsule\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ability Capsule\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. Allows a Pokémon of a species that has two possible Abilities (excluding Hidden Abilities) to change its Ability to the one it currently does not have.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-absorb-bulb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Absorb Bulb\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will raise the holder's Sp. Atk by 1 stage if it is hit with a damage-dealing Water-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on Route 5\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-adamant-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Adamant Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Attack to grow more easily while its Sp. Atk will grow more slowly"
".\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-adrenaline-orb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Adrenaline Orb\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Speed when affected by Intimidate.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-adventure-guide\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Adventure Guide\",\"body\":\"Description: A device that automatically collects and records advice during your adventure.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventure\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-aguav-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Aguav Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to rest"
"ore some HP when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower. It restores 1/3 of max HP but also confuses Pokémon that don't like bitter flavors.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 9 (Circhester Bay)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-air-balloon\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Air Balloon\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will grant immunity to all Ground-type moves until the holder is hit by a damage-dealing move.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Wyndon\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-amulet-coin\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Amulet Coin\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If a Pokémon holding it appears in battle, this item will double the prize money received from that battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in the Motostoke Outskirts\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-antidote\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Antidote\",\"bod"
"y\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will heal the poisoned and badly poisoned status conditions.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-apicot-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Apicot Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to raise its Sp. Def by 1 stage when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-aspear-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Aspear Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to cure itself of the frozen status condition during battle. Using this Berry on a Pokémon directly can also cure the frozen status condition.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 7 (north side)\",\"citation\":\"Official S"
"word/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-assault-vest\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Assault Vest\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Sp. Def by 50% but prevent the Pokémon from using status moves.\\nMain way to obtain: Find at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-awakening\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Awakening\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will heal the asleep status condition.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-babiri-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Babiri Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Steel-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree in the area surrounded by the lake in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\""
",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-balm-mushroom\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Balm Mushroom\",\"body\":\"Description: A fragrant mushroom. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item near trees in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-beast-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Beast Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Ultra Beasts that appear in other regions. It's not very effective at catching regular Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-berry-juice\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Berry Juice\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds this item, it can drink the juice to restore 20 HP during battle when its HP drops to 1/2 of its maximum or lower.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Ba"
"ttle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-berry-sweet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Berry Sweet\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Milcery evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-big-malasada\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Big Malasada\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. This famous fried bread from the Alola region can be used to heal a Pokémon of any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-big-mushroom\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Big Mushroom\",\"body\":\"Description: A big mushroom. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item near trees in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-big-nugget\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Big Nugget\",\"body\":\"Desc"
"ription: A big nugget of pure gold. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 8 or in Wyndon\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-big-pearl\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Big Pearl\",\"body\":\"Description: A big pearl. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item near or on the lakes in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-big-root\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Big Root\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will increase the amount of HP restored to the holder by HP-draining moves by 30%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in the Glimwood Tangle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-binding-band\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Binding Band\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the effectiveness of the holder's binding moves. They will damage the "
"target for 1/6 of its max HP each turn, instead of the regular 1/8.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-black-belt\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Black Belt\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Fighting-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on Route 9 (Circhester Bay)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-black-glasses\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Black Glasses\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Dark-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Motostoke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-black-sludge\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Black Sludge\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Poison-type Pokémon, this item will restore 1/16 of "
"the holder's max HP each turn. If held by any other type, it will cause the holder to lose 1/8 of its max HP each turn.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in Wyndon\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-blunder-policy\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Blunder Policy\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will raise the holder's Speed by 2 stages if one of its moves misses due to low accuracy.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-bold-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Bold Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Defense to grow more easily while its Attack will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide,"
" pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-bottle-cap\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Bottle Cap\",\"body\":\"Description: A beautiful bottle cap that gives off a silver gleam. Use one to have a Lv. 100 Pokémon train up one stat via Hyper Training.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-brave-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Brave Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Attack to grow more easily while its Speed will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-bright-powder\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Bright Powder\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will lower the accuracy of moves that target the holder.\\nMain way to obtai"
"n: Find in Glimwood Tangle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-bug-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Bug Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Bug type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-burn-heal\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Burn Heal\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will heal the burned status condition.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-calcium\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Calcium\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add base points to the Pokémon's Sp. Atk stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Wyndon's southern Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–38"
"0\"},{\"key\":\"items-calm-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Calm Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Sp. Def to grow more easily while its Attack will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-camping-gear\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Camping Gear\",\"body\":\"Description: A set of camping gear, including the equipment you need to cook at camp.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventure\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-carbos\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Carbos\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add base points to the Pokémon's Speed stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Wyndon's southern Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"ite"
"ms-careful-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Careful Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Sp. Def to grow more easily while its Sp. Atk will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-casteliacone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Casteliacone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. This famous ice cream from Castelia City can be used to heal a Pokémon of any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-catching-charm\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Catching Charm\",\"body\":\"Description: A curious charm said to increase the likelihood of catching Pokémon as a critical catch in the wild. Simply possessing one awards a Trainer with its effects.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the game"
" director in Circhester's Hotel Ionia\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-cell-battery\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Cell Battery\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will raise the holder's Attack by 1 stage if it is hit with ■ damage-dealing Electric-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Wyndon\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-charcoal\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Charcoal\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Fire-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Receive from Leon in Motostoke if you chose Scorbunny / Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-charti-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Charti Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffecti"
"ve Rock-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-cheri-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Cheri Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to cure itself of the paralysis status condition during battle. Using this Berry on a Pokémon directly can also cure the paralysis status condition.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at Wedgehurst Berry Grocer / Collect from the Berry trees in the Rolling Fields in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-chesto-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Chesto Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to cure itself of the asleep status condition during battle. Using this Berry on a Pokémon directly can also cure the asleep status condition.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Rout"
"e 5\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-chilan-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Chilan Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one Normal-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry trees near West Lake Axewell in the Dappled Grove in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-chipped-pot\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Chipped Pot\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help certain Sinistea evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-choice-band\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Choice Band\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Attack by 50%. However, the holder will become unable to use any move but the first move it chooses when it enters the batt"
"lefield.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 2\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-choice-scarf\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Choice Scarf\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Speed by 50%. However, the holder will become unable to use any move but the first move it chooses when it enters the battlefield.\\nMain way to obtain: Get by helping deliver an Old Letter for a little girl in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-choice-specs\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Choice Specs\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Sp. Atk by 50%. However, the holder will become unable to use any move but the first move it chooses when it enters the battlefield.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Spikemuth\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-chople-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\""
":\"Chople Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Fighting-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 9 (Outer Spikemuth)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-cleanse-tag\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Cleanse Tag\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by the lead Pokémon in your party, this item will reduce wild Pokémon encounters.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 4\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-clever-feather\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Clever Feather\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add a small number of base points to the Pokémon's Sp. Def stat. It can be used until base points for that stat have been maxed.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on the bridge on Route 5 or the bridge in the Motostoke Outskirts\",\"citation\""
":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-clover-sweet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Clover Sweet\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Milcery evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-coba-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Coba Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Flying-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree by the river at the Motostoke Riverbank in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-colbur-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Colbur Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Dark-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Axew's Eye in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":"
"\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-comet-shard\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Comet Shard\",\"body\":\"Description: A shard that fell to the ground when a comet passed by. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the North Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-cracked-pot\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Cracked Pot\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help certain Sinistea evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Stow-on-Side / Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-damp-rock\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Damp Rock\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If a Pokémon holding this item causes the weather condition to change to rain, the rain will last 8 turns instead of 5.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a gentleman in a house in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key"
"\":\"items-dark-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dark Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Dark type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dawn-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dawn Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Kirlia or Snorunt evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-destiny-knot\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Destiny Knot\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If a Pokémon holding this item is afflicted with infatuation, the Pokémon that caused it will also become infatuated.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, p"
"p. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-destiny-knot-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Destiny Knot\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help ensure that Pokémon Eggs you find inherit five individual strengths from the Pokémon you leave at the Nursery.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dire-hit\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dire Hit\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, it becomes much more likely the Pokémon will deliver critical hits.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dive-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dive Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon that live in the water or that are encountered on the water's surface.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Bu"
"y in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dragon-fang\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dragon Fang\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Dragon-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dragon-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dragon Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Dragon type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dream-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dream Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon when they are asleep.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from the Ball Gu"
"y in Wyndon\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dusk-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dusk Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon at night or in dark places such as caves.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Buy in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dusk-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dusk Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Lampent or Doublade evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dynamax-band\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dynamax Band\",\"body\":\"Description: A wristband that allows a Trainer to Dynamax their Pokémon at a Power Spot.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventure\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield"
" guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-dynamax-candy\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Dynamax Candy\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will raise the Pokémon's Dynamax Level by 1.\\nMain way to obtain: Find after a Max Raid Battle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-eject-button\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Eject Button\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will force the holder to switch out of battle if it is hit by a damage-dealing move.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-eject-pack\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Eject Pack\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will force the holder to switch out of battle if any of its stats are lowered.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Sh"
"op after becoming Champion; Find in Wyndon / Sometimes held by wild Togedemaru\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-electric-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Electric Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Electric type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-electric-seed\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Electric Seed\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Defense by 1 stage on Electric Terrain.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-elixir\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Elixir\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the PP of all its moves by 10 points each.\\nHow to obtain: Find as a hidden item on Route 8"
" / Pickup Ability\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-endorsement\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Endorsement\",\"body\":\"Description: A letter you need in order to participate in the Gym Challenge.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventure\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-energy-powder\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Energy Powder\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 60 points. However, the very bitter taste will make the Pokémon less friendly.\\nHow to obtain: Buy from the Herb Shop in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-energy-root\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Energy Root\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 120 points. However, the very bitter taste will make the Pokémon less friendly.\\nHow to obtain: Buy fro"
"m the Herb Shop in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-escape-rope\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Escape Rope\",\"body\":\"Description: A rope that can be used over and over to help you escape from locations like caves or dungeons.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventure\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ether\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ether\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the PP of one of its moves by 10 points.\\nHow to obtain: Find as a hidden item in Galar Mine or on Route 4 / Pickup Ability\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-everstone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Everstone\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will prevent the holder from evolving.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in Turffield\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, "
"pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-everstone-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Everstone\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help ensure that Pokémon Eggs you find inherit regional forms or Natures from the Pokémon you leave at the Nursery.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in Turffield\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-eviolite\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Eviolite\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the Defense and Sp. Def of the holder by 50% each as long as that Pokémon is still capable of evolving.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Breeder in a house in Ballonlea\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-exp-candy-l\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy L\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, it will award a large amount of Exp. Points.\\nMain way to obtain: Find after a Max Raid Battle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shiel"
"d guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-exp-candy-m\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy M\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, it will award a moderate amount of Exp. Points.\\nMain way to obtain: Find after a Max Raid Battle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-exp-candy-s\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy S\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, it will award a small amount of Exp. Points.\\nMain way to obtain: Find after a Max Raid Battle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-exp-candy-xl\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy XL\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, it will award a very large amount of Exp. Points.\\nMain way to obtain: Find after a Max Raid Battle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-exp-candy-xs\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Exp. Candy XS\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on"
" a Pokémon, it will award a very small amount of Exp. Points.\\nMain way to obtain: Find after a Max Raid Battle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-expert-belt\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Expert Belt\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's supereffective moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find by solving a riddle in Turffield\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fairy-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fairy Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Fairy type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fast-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fast Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon th"
"at have a high Speed stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one as a reward after completing a Rotom Rally course for the eleventh time.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fighting-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fighting Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Fighting type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-figy-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Figy Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to restore some HP when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower. It restores 1/3 of max HP but also confuses Pokémon that don't like spicy flavors.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 7 (north side)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-f"
"ire-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fire Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Fire type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fire-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fire Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Vulpix, Growlithe, or Eevee evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fishing-rod\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fishing Rod\",\"body\":\"Description: A fishing rod that allows you to fish up Pokémon living in the water.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventure\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-flame-orb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Flame Orb"
"\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will inflict the burned status condition on the holder.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward in a Champion tournament after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-float-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Float Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's weight.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the Digging Duo in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-flower-sweet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Flower Sweet\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Milcery evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-flying-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Flying Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's typ"
"e to Flying type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-focus-band\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Focus Band\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will give the holder a 10% chance of surviving with 1 HP when it receives damage that would normally cause it to faint.\\nMain way to obtain: Sometimes held by wild Machop, Machoke, and Machamp\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-focus-sash\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Focus Sash\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon with full HP, this item will allow the holder to survive with 1 HP when it receives damage that would normally cause it to faint.\\nMain way to obtain: Find at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fossilized-bird\",\"category\":"
"\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fossilized Bird\",\"body\":\"Description: The fossil of an ancient Pokémon that once soared through the sky. It can be restored, together with another fossil, to obtain certain Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the Dusty Bowl in the Wild Area ↑ / Get from the Digging Duo in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fossilized-dino\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fossilized Dino\",\"body\":\"Description: The fossil of an ancient Pokémon that once lived in the sea. It can be restored, together with another fossil, to obtain certain Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the Dusty Bowl in the Wild Area ↑ / Get from the Digging Duo in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fossilized-drake\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fossilized Drake\",\"body\":\"Description: The fossil of an ancient Pokémon that once roamed the land. It can be restored, together with another fossi"
"l, to obtain certain Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the Dusty Bowl in the Wild Area ♥ / Get from the Digging Duo in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fossilized-fish\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fossilized Fish\",\"body\":\"Description: The fossil of an ancient Pokémon that once lived in the sea. It can be restored, together with another fossil, to obtain certain Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the Dusty Bowl in the Wild Area ♥ / Get from the Digging Duo in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-fresh-water\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Fresh Water\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 30 points.\\nHow to obtain: Buy from a vending machine in a train station\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-friend-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Friend Ball\",\"body"
"\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It will immediately make a Pokémon caught with it more friendly toward you.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from the Ball Guy in Turffield\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-full-heal\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Full Heal\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will heal any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 6 Gym Badges\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-full-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Full Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will make the holder move later in the turn. It can also be used to help find Pokémon Eggs that hatch into certain species.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-full-incense-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Full Incense\",\"body\":\"Des"
"cription: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help you find a Pokémon Egg that will hatch into a Munchlax.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-full-restore\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Full Restore\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will fully restore the Pokémon's HP and cure any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 8 Gym Badges\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ganlon-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ganlon Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to raise its Defense by 1 stage when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree in the area surrounded by the lake in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-"
"genius-feather\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Genius Feather\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add a small number of base points to the Pokémon's Sp. Atk stat. It can be used until base points for that stat have been maxed.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on the bridge on Route 5 or the bridge in the Motostoke Outskirts\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-gentle-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Gentle Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Sp. Def to grow more easily while its Defense will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ghost-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ghost Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to "
"Ghost type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-gold-bottle-cap\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Gold Bottle Cap\",\"body\":\"Description: A beautiful bottle cap that gives off a golden gleam. Use one to have a Lv. 100 Pokémon train up all six stats via Hyper Training.\\nMain way to obtain: Receive as a prize in Ranked Battles at the Battle Tower\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-grass-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Grass Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Grass type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-grassy-seed\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Grassy Seed\",\"body\":\"Description: A consum"
"able item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Defense by 1 stage on Grassy Terrain.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Wyndon\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-great-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Great Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is more likely to successfully catch a Pokémon than a basic Poké Ball.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 1 Gym Badge\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-grepa-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Grepa Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this Berry will make that Pokémon more friendly, but it will also take away base points from its Sp. Def stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the left Berry tree under the bridge in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-grip-claw\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Grip Claw\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonco"
"nsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will extend the duration of the holder's moves like Bind and Wrap to 7 turns.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Galar Mine No. 2\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ground-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ground Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Ground type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-guard-spec\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Guard Spec.\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used during battle, this item will prevent stat reduction among the Trainer's party Pokémon for 5 turns. Cannot be used again until the effect wears off.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-haban-berry\","
"\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Haban Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Dragon-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-hard-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Hard Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Rock-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find it as a hidden item in Galar Mine\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-hasty-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Hasty Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Speed to grow more easily while its Defense will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citati"
"on\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-heal-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Heal Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It will fully restore the HP and PP of the Pokémon caught with it and heal any status conditions.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Buy in Motostoke's lower Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-heal-powder\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Heal Powder\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will heal the Pokémon of any status condition or confusion. However, the very bitter taste will make the Pokémon less friendly.\\nHow to obtain: Buy from the Herb Shop in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-health-feather\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Health Feather\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add a small number of base points to the Pokémon's HP. It can"
" be used until base points for that stat have been maxed.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on the bridge on Route 5 or the bridge in the Motostoke Outskirts\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-heat-rock\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Heat Rock\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If a Pokémon holding this item causes the weather condition to change to harsh sunlight, the harsh sunlight will last 8 turns instead of 5.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a gentleman in a house in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-heavy-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Heavy Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon that weigh a lot.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from the Ball Guy in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-heavy-duty-boots\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Heavy-Duty Boots\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item"
". If held by a Pokémon, this item will protect the holder from the effects of Spikes, Stealth Rock, Sticky Web, and Toxic Spikes.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Galar Mine\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-hi-tech-earbuds\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Hi-tech Earbuds\",\"body\":\"Description: Strange earbuds that allow you to adjust the volume of various sounds in the Options.\\nMain way to obtain: Talk to a man on the street near the eastern record shop in Motostoke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-hondew-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Hondew Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this Berry will make that Pokémon more friendly, but it will also take away base points from its Sp. Atk stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the left Berry tree under the bridge in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-honey\",\"category\":\"Item"
"s\",\"title\":\"Honey\",\"body\":\"Description: A sweet honey collected by wild Pokémon. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in flower patches in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-hp-up\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"HP Up\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add base points to the Pokémon's HP stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Wyndon's southern Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-hyper-potion\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Hyper Potion\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 120 points.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 4 Gym Badges\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-iapapa-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Iapapa Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this "
"Berry to restore some HP when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower. It restores 1/3 of max HP but also confuses Pokémon that don't like sour flavors.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 9 (Circhester Bay)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ice-heal\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ice Heal\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will heal the frozen status condition.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ice-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ice Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Ice type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ice-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ice Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consu"
"mable item. It can be used to help Eevee evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-icy-rock\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Icy Rock\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If a Pokémon holding this item causes the weather condition to change to hail, the hail will last 8 turns instead of 5.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a gentleman in a house in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-impish-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Impish Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Defense to grow more easily while its Sp. Atk will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-iron\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Iron\",\"body\":\"Descrip"
"tion: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add base points to the Pokémon's Defense stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Wyndon's southern Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-iron-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Iron Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will reduce the holder's Speed stat by 50%. If the holder is a Flying-type Pokémon or has the Levitate Ability, it will also lose its immunity to Ground-type moves.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the Digging Duo in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-jolly-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Jolly Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Speed to grow more easily while its Sp. Atk will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Offi"
"cial Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-kasib-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Kasib Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Ghost-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree in the area surrounded by the lake in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-kebia-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Kebia Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Poison-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Axew's Eye in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-kee-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Kee Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to raise its Defense by 1 stage when hit with a physica"
"l move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Axew's Eye in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-kelpsy-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Kelpsy Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this Berry will make that Pokémon more friendly, but it will also take away base points from its Attack stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the right Berry tree under the bridge in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-king-s-rock\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"King's Rock\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, the holder may cause targets to flinch when dealing damage.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 8 / Sometimes held by wild Hawlucha; Get from the Digging Duo in the Wild Area / Sometimes held by wild Cufant and Copperajah\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lagging-tail\",\"category\":"
"\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lagging Tail\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will cause the holder to move later.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lansat-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lansat Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to make itself more likely to deliver critical hits when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward at the Battle Tower\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lava-cookie\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lava Cookie\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. This famous treat from Lavaridge Town can be used to heal a Pokémon of any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lax-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lax Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. "
"If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's evasiveness. It can also be used to help find Pokémon Eggs that hatch into certain species.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lax-incense-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lax Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help you find a Pokémon Egg that will hatch into a Wynaut.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lax-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lax Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Defense to grow more easily while its Sp. Def will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-leaf-stone\",\"category\":\""
"Items\",\"title\":\"Leaf Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Gloom, Eevee, or Nuzleaf evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-leek\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Leek\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Farfetch'd, this item will make the Farfetch'd much more likely to deliver critical hits.\\nMain way to obtain: Sometimes held by wild Farfetch'd and Sirfetch'd\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-leftovers\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Leftovers\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will restore 1/16 of the holder's max HP each turn.\\nMain way to obtain: Find at the Giant's Seat in the Wild Area / Get from a Berry tree in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lemonade\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lemonade"
"\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 70 points.\\nHow to obtain: Buy from a vending machine in a train station\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-leppa-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Leppa Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to restore 10 points to the PP of one of its moves.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree near the Lake of Outrage on the Hammerlocke Hills in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-level-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Level Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon that are lower in level than your own.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from the Ball Guy in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-liechi-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Liechi Berry\",\"body\":\"D"
"escription: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to raise its Attack by 1 stage when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree in the area surrounded by the lake in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-life-orb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Life Orb\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, the holder will lose HP each time it attacks, but the power of its moves will be boosted by 30%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in the Slumbering Weald\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-light-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Light Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pikachu, this item will double the Pikachu's Attack and Sp. Atk.\\nMain way to obtain: Sometimes held by wild Pikachu\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-light-ball-2\",\"category\":\""
"Items\",\"title\":\"Light Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help you find a Pokémon Egg that will hatch into a Pichu that knows the move Volt Tackle.\\nMain way to obtain: Sometimes held by wild Pikachu\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-light-clay\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Light Clay\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will extend the duration of the moves Aurora Veil, Light Screen, and Reflect by 3 turns.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 6\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lonely-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lonely Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Attack to grow more easily while its Defense will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380"
"\"},{\"key\":\"items-love-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Love Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon that are the same species as and the opposite gender to your active Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from the Ball Guy in Ballonlea\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-love-sweet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Love Sweet\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Milcery evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-luck-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Luck Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If a Pokémon holding it appears in battle, this item will double the prize money received from that battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lucky-egg\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lucky Egg"
"\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, the holder will gain 50% more Exp. Points from battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a chef by helping him in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lum-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lum Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to cure itself of any status condition or confusion during battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 9 (Outer Spikemuth)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-luminous-moss\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Luminous Moss\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will raise the holder's Sp. Def by 1 stage if it is hit with a damage-dealing Water-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Glimwood Tangle\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lumiose-galette\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lumiose G"
"alette\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. This popular pastry from Lumiose City can be used to heal a Pokémon of any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-lure-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Lure Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon that have been fished up with a fishing rod.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from the Ball Guy in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-luxury-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Luxury Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It makes a Pokémon caught with it quickly become more friendly toward you.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Buy in Wyndon's southern Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-macho-brace\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Macho Brace\",\"body\":\"Description"
": A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-macho-brace-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Macho Brace\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-magnet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Magnet\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Electric-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-mago-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Mago Berry\","
"\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to restore some HP when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower. It restores 1/3 of max HP but also confuses Pokémon that don't like sweet flavors.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 7 (north side)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-maranga-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Maranga Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to raise its Sp. Def by 1 stage when hit with a special move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Axew's Eye in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-master-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Master Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A very rare type of Poké Ball. It is guaranteed to catch any wild Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from Professor Magnolia after becoming Champion / Win one in the Loto-ID if you're v"
"ery lucky\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-max-elixir\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Max Elixir\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the PP of all its moves completely.\\nHow to obtain: Find as a hidden item on Route 9 / Pickup Ability\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-max-ether\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Max Ether\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the PP of one of its moves completely.\\nHow to obtain: Find as a hidden item on Route 2 / Pickup Ability\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-max-potion\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Max Potion\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will fully restore the Pokémon's HP.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 7 Gym Badges; Find in the Watchtower Ruins in the Wild Area, on Routes 8, 9, or 10, or in"
" Spikemuth / Pickup Ability\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-max-repel\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Max Repel\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If you use it, this item will prevent you from encountering lower-level Pokémon in the wild. The effect lasts longer than a Super Repel.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 7 Gym Badges\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-max-revive\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Max Revive\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a fainted Pokémon, this item will revive the Pokémon and fully restore its HP.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-mental-herb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Mental Herb\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, the holder will instantly shake off the effects of Attract, Disable, Encore, Taunt, and Torment, as well as Abilities that inflict similar effects.\\nMain way to obtain:"
" Find in the Slumbering Weald\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-metal-coat\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Metal Coat\",\"body\":\"Description: An item with different uses. It can be used to help Onix evolve. When used in this way, the item will be consumed.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-metal-coat-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Metal Coat\",\"body\":\"Description: An item with different uses. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Steel-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-metal-powder\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Metal Powder\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Ditto, this item will double the Ditto's Defense.\\nMain way to obtain: Sometimes held by wild Ditto\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp"
". 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-metronome\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Metronome\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of a move used consecutively by the holder. The power increases with each use until it reaches the max of 200%.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-mild-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Mild Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Sp. Atk to grow more easily while its Defense will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-miracle-seed\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Miracle Seed\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Grass-type moves by 20%.\\n"
"Main way to obtain: Receive from Leon in Motostoke if you chose Grookey / Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-misty-seed\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Misty Seed\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Sp. Def by 1 stage on Misty Terrain.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in the Slumbering Weald\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-modest-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Modest Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Sp. Atk to grow more easily while its Attack will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-moomoo-milk\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Moomoo Milk\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, t"
"his item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 100 points.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-moon-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Moon Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon that can be evolved using a Moon Stone.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one from the Ball Guy in Circhester\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-moon-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Moon Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Clefairy or Munna evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in the Dusty Bowl in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-muscle-band\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Muscle Band\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's physical moves by 10%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Officia"
"l Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-muscle-feather\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Muscle Feather\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add a small number of base points to the Pokémon's Attack stat. It can be used until base points for that stat have been maxed.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on the bridge on Route 5 or the bridge in the Motostoke Outskirts\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-mystic-water\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Mystic Water\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Water-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Receive from Leon in Motostoke if you chose Sobble / Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-naughty-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Naughty Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item "
"will cause the Pokémon's Attack to grow more easily while its Sp. Def will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-na-ve-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Naïve Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Speed to grow more easily while its Sp. Def will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-nest-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Nest Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon of lower levels.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Buy in Motostoke's lower Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-net-ball\",\"categ"
"ory\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Net Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Water- or Bug-type Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Buy in Motostoke's lower Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-never-melt-ice\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Never-Melt Ice\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Ice-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on Route 9 (Circhester Bay)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-normal-gem\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Normal Gem\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of a Normal-type move used by the holder by 30%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on Route 9 (Circhester Bay)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-nugget\",\"category"
"\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Nugget\",\"body\":\"Description: A nugget of pure gold. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in Motostoke, Hammerlocke, or elsewhere\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-occa-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Occa Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Fire-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the center Berry tree under the bridge in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-odd-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Odd Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Psychic-type moves by 20%. It can also be used to help find Pokémon Eggs that hatch into certain species.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official "
"Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-odd-incense-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Odd Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help you find a Pokémon Egg that will hatch into a Mime Jr.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-old-gateau\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Old Gateau\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. This secret specialty of the Old Chateau can be used to heal a Pokémon of any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-oran-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Oran Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to restore 10 HP when its HP drops to 1/2 of its maximum or lower.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at Wedgehurst Berry Grocer / Collect from the Berry trees in the Rolling Fields in the Wild A"
"rea\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-oval-charm\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Oval Charm\",\"body\":\"Description: An oval charm said to increase the chance of Pokémon Eggs being found at the Nursery. Simply possessing one awards a Trainer with its effects.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from Morimoto if you defeat him in a battle at Circhester's Hotel Ionia after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-paralyze-heal\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Paralyze Heal\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will heal the paralysis status condition.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-passho-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Passho Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Water-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect fr"
"om the right Berry tree in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-payapa-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Payapa Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Psychic-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree near the Lake of Outrage on the Hammerlocke Hills in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pearl\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Pearl\",\"body\":\"Description: A pretty pearl. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item near or on the lakes in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pearl-string\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Pearl String\",\"body\":\"Description: A string of large pearls with a silvery sheen. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item nea"
"r or on the lakes in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pecha-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Pecha Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to cure itself of the poisoned or badly poisoned status condition during battle. Using this Berry on a Pokémon directly can also cure the poisoned status condition.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at Wedgehurst Berry Grocer / Collect from the Berry tree near the Meetup Spot in the Rolling Fields in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-persim-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Persim Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to cure itself of confusion during battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree at North Lake Miloch in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-petaya-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"ti"
"tle\":\"Petaya Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to raise its Sp. Atk by 1 stage when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pewter-crunchies\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Pewter Crunchies\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. This famous snack from Pewter City can be used to heal a Pokémon of any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-poison-barb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Poison Barb\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Poison-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-poi"
"son-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Poison Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Poison type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pok-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Poké Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is the most basic model and is decently successful at catching wild Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart after you meet up with Leon on Route 2\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pok-doll\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Poké Doll\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used in a battle against a wild Pokémon, this item ends the battle instantly.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 1 Gym Badge\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pok-mon-box-"
"link\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Pokémon Box Link\",\"body\":\"Description: A device that allows you to access your Boxes in the Pokémon storage system even when you're out and about.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventure\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pomeg-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Pomeg Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this Berry will make that Pokémon more friendly, but it will also take away base points from its HP stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the center Berry tree under the bridge in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-potion\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Potion\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 20 points.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-p"
"ower-anklet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Anklet\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Speed stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-anklet-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Anklet\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Speed stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-anklet-3\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Anklet\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help ensure that Pokémon Eggs you find inherit the Speed individual strength from the Pokémon you leave at the"
" Nursery.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-band\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Band\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Sp. Def stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-band-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Band\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Sp. Def stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-band-3\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Band\",\"body\":\"Descript"
"ion: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help ensure that Pokémon Eggs you find inherit the Sp. Def individual strength from the Pokémon you leave at the Nursery.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-belt\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Belt\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Defense stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-belt-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Belt\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Defense stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's centra"
"l Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-belt-3\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Belt\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help ensure that Pokémon Eggs you find inherit the Defense individual strength from the Pokémon you leave at the Nursery.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-bracer\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Bracer\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Attack stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-bracer-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Bracer\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will "
"halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Attack stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-bracer-3\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Bracer\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help ensure that Pokémon Eggs you find inherit the Attack individual strength from the Pokémon you leave at the Nursery.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-herb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Herb\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, the holder will be able to immediately use a move that would normally require one turn to charge.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide,"
" pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-lens\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Lens\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Sp. Atk stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-lens-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Lens\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its Sp. Atk stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-lens-3\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Lens\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help ensure that Pokémon Eggs you find inherit the Sp. Atk individual strength from the "
"Pokémon you leave at the Nursery.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-weight\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Weight\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its HP stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-weight-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Power Weight\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will halve the holder's Speed but increase the rate at which it gains base points for its HP stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-power-weight-3\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Powe"
"r Weight\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help ensure that Pokémon Eggs you find inherit the HP individual strength from the Pokémon you leave at the Nursery.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pp-max\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"PP Max\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item can increase the max PP of one of the Pokémon's moves as high as it will go.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 2 / Get as a reward at the Battle Tower\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pp-up\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"PP Up\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item can increase the max PP of one of the Pokémon's moves by a small amount.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the Motostoke Outskirts, on Route 7, or elsewhere\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guid"
"e, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-premier-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Premier Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball made to celebrate a special event of some sort. It is as effective as a basic Poké Ball.\\nMain way to obtain: Get one each time you buy 10 Poké Balls at a Poké Mart\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pretty-feather\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Pretty Feather\",\"body\":\"Description: A beautiful feather. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on the bridge on Route 5 or the bridge in the Motostoke Outskirts\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-prism-scale\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Prism Scale\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Feebas evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on Route 2\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-protective-pads\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Protective Pads\",\"b"
"ody\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will protect the holder from effects caused by making direct contact with a target.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-protector\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Protector\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Rhydon evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 9 (Circhester Bay)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-protein\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Protein\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add base points to the Pokémon's Attack stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-psychic-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Psychic Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will"
" change Silvally's type to Psychic type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-psychic-seed\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Psychic Seed\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's Sp. Def by 1 stage on Psychic Terrain.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 2\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-pure-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Pure Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by the lead Pokémon in your party, this item will reduce wild Pokémon encounters.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-qualot-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Qualot Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this Berry will make that Pokémon mor"
"e friendly, but it will also take away base points from its Defense stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the right Berry tree under the bridge in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-quick-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Quick Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon on the first turn in battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Buy in Wyndon's southern Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-quick-claw\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Quick Claw\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will occasionally allow the holder to strike with high priority.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-quick-powder\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Quick Powder\",\"body\":\"Description: A non"
"consumable item. If held by a Ditto, this item will double the Ditto's Speed.\\nMain way to obtain: Sometimes held by wild Ditto\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-quiet-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Quiet Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Sp. Atk to grow more easily while its Speed will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rage-candy-bar\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rage Candy Bar\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. This famous snack from Mahogany Town can be used to heal a Pokémon of any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rare-bone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rare Bone\",\"body\":\"Description: A rare bone. It c"
"an be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the Dusty Bowl or at the Giant's Mirror in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rare-candy\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rare Candy\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will raise the Pokémon's level by 1.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center / Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rash-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rash Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Sp. Atk to grow more easily while its Sp. Def will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rawst-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rawst Berry\",\"bo"
"dy\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to cure itself of the burned status condition during battle. Using this Berry on a Pokémon directly can also cure the burned status condition.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree at North Lake Miloch in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-razor-claw\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Razor Claw\",\"body\":\"Description: An item with different uses. It can be used to help Sneasel evolve. When used in this way, the item will be consumed.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the Dusty Bowl in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-razor-claw-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Razor Claw\",\"body\":\"Description: An item with different uses. If held by a Pokémon, the holder will become much more likely to deliver critical hits.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the Dusty Bowl in the Wild Area\",\"citati"
"on\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-reaper-cloth\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Reaper Cloth\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Dusclops evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get by helping deliver an Old Letter for a little girl in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-red-card\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Red Card\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, any other Pokémon that hits the holder with a damage-dealing move will be forced to switch out.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-relaxed-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Relaxed Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Defense to grow more easily while its Speed will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-h"
"and clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-repeat-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Repeat Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching a species of Pokémon that you've caught at least once before.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Buy in Wyndon's southern Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-repel\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Repel\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If you use it, this item will prevent you from encountering lower-level Pokémon in the wild.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 3 Gym Badges\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-resist-feather\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Resist Feather\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add a small number of base points to the Pokémo"
"n's Defense stat. It can be used until base points for that stat have been maxed.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on the bridge on Route 5 or the bridge in the Motostoke Outskirts\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-revival-herb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Revival Herb\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to revive a Pokémon that has fainted. However, the very bitter taste will make the Pokémon less friendly.\\nHow to obtain: Buy from the Herb Shop in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-revive\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Revive\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a fainted Pokémon, this item will revive the Pokémon and restore half of its max HP.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ribbon-sweet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ribbon Sweet\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to h"
"elp Milcery evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rindo-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rindo Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Grass-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the left Berry tree under the bridge in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ring-target\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ring Target\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, moves that would usually deal no damage to the holder due to type matchups will instead deal regular damage.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rock-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rock Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a"
" Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Rock-type moves by 20%. It can also be used to help find Pokémon Eggs that hatch into certain species.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rock-incense-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rock Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help you find a Pokémon Egg that will hatch into a Bonsly.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rock-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rock Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Rock type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rocky-helmet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"R"
"ocky Helmet\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, any other Pokémon that uses a move that makes direct contact with the holder will lose 1/6 of its max HP.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-room-service\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Room Service\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will lower the holder's Speed by 1 stage if Trick Room is used.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rose-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rose Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Grass-type moves by 20%. It can also be used to help find Pokémon Eggs that hatch into certain species.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"c"
"itation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rose-incense-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rose Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help you find a Pokémon Egg that will hatch into a Budew.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-roseli-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Roseli Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Fairy-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 9 (Outer Spikemuth)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rotom-bike\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rotom Bike\",\"body\":\"Description: A bike that has been powered up by the Pokémon Rotom. With the right parts, it can run over water as well as on land.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventu"
"re\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rotom-catalog\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rotom Catalog\",\"body\":\"Description: A catalog of devices that Rotom like. It can be used to have a Rotom change form.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom user in Wyndon\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rusted-shield\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rusted Shield\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Zamazenta, this item will change it to its Crowned Shield form.\\nMain way to obtain: Obtain during your main adventure ❤\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-rusted-sword\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Rusted Sword\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Zacian, this item will change it to its Crowned Sword form.\\nMain way to obtain: Obtain during your main adventure ↑\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-sachet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sachet\""
",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Spritzee evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-safety-goggles\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Safety Goggles\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, the holder will be protected from weather-related damage, certain moves (Cotton Spore, Magic Powder, Poison Powder, Rage Powder, Sleep Powder, Spore, and Stun Spore), and from the Effect Spore Ability.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 7\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-salac-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Salac Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to raise its Speed by 1 stage when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Axew's Eye in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shiel"
"d guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-sassy-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sassy Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Sp. Def to grow more easily while its Speed will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-scope-lens\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Scope Lens\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, it becomes much more likely the holder will deliver critical hits.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 9 (Outer Spikemuth)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-sea-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sea Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Water-type moves by 20%. It can also be used to help find Pokémon Eggs that hatch into certain spe"
"cies.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-serious-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Serious Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's stats to grow at an equal rate.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-shalour-sable\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Shalour Sable\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. This famous shortbread from Shalour City can be used to heal a Pokémon of any status condition or confusion.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-sharp-beak\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sharp Beak\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Flying-type m"
"oves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 4\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-shed-shell\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Shed Shell\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will allow the holder to switch out even when trapped by the effects of moves or Abilities.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 5\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-shell-bell\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Shell Bell\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will restore the holder's HP when it hits another Pokémon with a damage-dealing move. The holder will regain HP equal to 1/8 of the damage dealt.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-shiny-charm\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Shiny Charm\",\"body\":\"Description: A shiny charm said to increase the chances of encountering Shiny Pokémon in the wild. Simply posses"
"sing one awards a Trainer with its effects.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the game director in Circhester's Hotel Ionia if you complete your Pokédex\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-shiny-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Shiny Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Togetic, Roselia, and Minccino evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-shuca-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Shuca Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Ground-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-silk-scarf\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Silk Scarf\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by"
" a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Normal-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Motostoke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-silver-powder\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Silver Powder\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Bug-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 4\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-sitrus-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sitrus Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to restore 1/2 of its max HP when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree by the river at the Motostoke Riverbank in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-smoke-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Smoke Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a P"
"okémon, this item will allow the holder to run away from wild Pokémon even when trapped by the effects of moves or Abilities.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in the Slumbering Weald\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-smooth-rock\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Smooth Rock\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If a Pokémon holding this item causes the weather condition to change to sandstorm, the sandstorm will last 8 turns instead of 5.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a gentleman in a house in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-snowball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Snowball\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will raise the holder's Attack by 1 stage if it is hit with a damage-dealing Ice-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Circhester\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-soda-pop\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Soda Pop\",\"body\":\"Description"
": A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 50 points.\\nHow to obtain: Buy from a vending machine in a train station\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-soft-sand\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Soft Sand\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Ground-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in Galar Mine No. 2\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-sonia-s-book\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sonia's Book\",\"body\":\"Description: Professor Sonia's published writings about the Galar region's legends.\\nMain way to obtain: Meet Sonia in the Slumbering Weald after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-soothe-bell\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Soothe Bell\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, the holder will become friendly m"
"ore quickly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a girl in a house in Motostoke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-spell-tag\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Spell Tag\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Ghost-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-star-piece\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Star Piece\",\"body\":\"Description: A sparkling red gem. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the North Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-star-sweet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Star Sweet\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Milcery evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-stardust\",\"categ"
"ory\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Stardust\",\"body\":\"Description: Lovely, red-colored sand. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item in the North Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-starf-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Starf Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to raise one of its stats by 2 stages when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower. The stat is selected at random.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward at the Battle Tower\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-steel-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Steel Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Steel type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-stic"
"ky-barb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sticky Barb\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will cause the holder to lose 1/8 of its max HP each turn. If another Pokémon uses a move that makes direct contact with the holder, this item will pass to the attacker.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the Digging Duo in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-strawberry-sweet\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Strawberry Sweet\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Milcery evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Hammerlocke / Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-sun-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sun Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Gloom, Cottonee, or Helioptile evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in the Dusty Bowl in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-"
"super-potion\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Super Potion\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 60 points.\\nHow to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 1 Gym Badge\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-super-repel\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Super Repel\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If you use it, this item will prevent you from encountering lower-level Pokémon in the wild. The effect lasts longer than a basic Repel.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 5 Gym Badges\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-sweet-apple\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sweet Apple\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Applin evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a guy in Hammerlocke by helping him ❤ / Find as a hidden item on Axew's Eye in the Wild Area ❤\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"item"
"s-sweet-heart\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Sweet Heart\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will restore the Pokémon's HP by 20 points.\\nHow to obtain: Get as a reward at a Battle Café\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-swift-feather\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Swift Feather\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will add a small number of base points to the Pokémon's Speed stat. It can be used until base points for that stat have been maxed.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item on the bridge on Route 5 or the bridge in the Motostoke Outskirts\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-tamato-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Tamato Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this Berry will make that Pokémon more friendly, but it will also take away base points from its Speed stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the cen"
"ter Berry tree under the bridge in the Bridge Field in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-tanga-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Tanga Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Bug-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 9 (Outer Spikemuth)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-tart-apple\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Tart Apple\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Applin evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a guy in Hammerlocke by helping him ↑ / Find as a hidden item on Axew's Eye in the Wild Area ↑\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-terrain-extender\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Terrain Extender\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, any terrain triggered by the holder's moves or Ability"
" will last 8 turns instead of 5.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 8\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-throat-spray\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Throat Spray\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will raise the holder's Sp. Atk by 1 stage if it uses a sound-based move in battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a boy by finding his Minccino in Motostoke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-thunder-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Thunder Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Pikachu or Eevee evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-timer-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Timer Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is most effective for catching Pokémon after many turns have passed in a battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Get fro"
"m a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area / Buy in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-timid-mint\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Timid Mint\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, this item will cause the Pokémon's Speed to grow more easily while its Attack will grow more slowly.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the left-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-tiny-mushroom\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Tiny Mushroom\",\"body\":\"Description: A tiny mushroom. It can be sold at shops for profit.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item near trees in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-toxic-orb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Toxic Orb\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will inflict the badly poisoned status condition on the holde"
"r during battle.\\nMain way to obtain: Get as a reward in a Champion tournament after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-twisted-spoon\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Twisted Spoon\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Psychic-type moves by 20%.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at the bargain stall in Stow-on-Side\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-ultra-ball\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Ultra Ball\",\"body\":\"Description: A type of Poké Ball. It is more likely to successfully catch a Pokémon than even a Great Ball.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy at any Poké Mart once you have 5 Gym Badges\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-utility-umbrella\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Utility Umbrella\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will negate the effects of both the rain and harsh s"
"unlight weather conditions.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a gentleman in a house in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-wacan-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Wacan Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Electric-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree near the Lake of Outrage on the Hammerlocke Hills in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-water-memory\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Water Memory\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by Silvally, this item will change Silvally's type to Water type.\\nMain way to obtain: Get Type: Null and all of Silvally's memory discs at the Battle Tower after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-water-stone\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Water Stone\",\"body\":\"Description: A con"
"sumable item. It can be used to help Shellder, Eevee, and Lombre evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Find as a hidden item at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-wave-incense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Wave Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's Water-type moves by 20%. It can also be used to help find Pokémon Eggs that hatch into certain species.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-wave-incense-2\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Wave Incense\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. It can be used to help you find a Pokémon Egg that will hatch into a Mantyke.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy from the Incense Merchant in Hulbury\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-weakness-policy\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Weakness Polic"
"y\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will increase the holder's Attack and Sp. Atk by 2 stages each if the holder is hit with a supereffective move.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the right-hand clerk at the Battle Tower's BP Shop after becoming Champion\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-whipped-dream\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Whipped Dream\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. It can be used to help Swirlix evolve.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from the BP Shop in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-white-herb\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"White Herb\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will restore any lowered stats one time.\\nMain way to obtain: Find at the Watchtower Ruins in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-wide-lens\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Wide Len"
"s\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's accuracy by 10%.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from Howses by solving a mystery in Circhester's Hotel Ionia\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-wiki-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Wiki Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to restore some HP when its HP drops to 1/4 of its maximum or lower. It restores 1/3 of max HP but also confuses Pokémon that don't like dry flavors.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree on Route 9 (Circhester Bay)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-wise-glasses\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Wise Glasses\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the power of the holder's special moves by 10%.\\nMain way to obtain: Find in Hammerlocke\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"k"
"ey\":\"items-wishing-piece\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Wishing Piece\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If you use one at a Pokémon Den, it may attract a wild Dynamax Pokémon.\\nMain way to obtain: Get from a Rotom Rallyist in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-wishing-star\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Wishing Star\",\"body\":\"Description: A stone with a mysterious power. It's said your dreams come true if you find one.\\nMain way to obtain: You'll obtain it automatically during your main adventure\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-x-accuracy\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"X Accuracy\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon during battle, this item will raise the accuracy of the Pokémon by 2 stages.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-x-attack\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"X Attack\",\"bod"
"y\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon during battle, this item will raise the Attack of the Pokémon by 2 stages.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Motostoke's lower Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-x-defense\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"X Defense\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon during battle, this item will raise the Defense of the Pokémon by 2 stages.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Motostoke's lower Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-x-sp-atk\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"X Sp. Atk\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon during battle, this item will raise the Sp. Atk of the Pokémon by 2 stages.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Motostoke's lower Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-x-sp-def\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"X Sp. Def\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a "
"Pokémon during battle, this item will raise the Sp. Def of the Pokémon by 2 stages.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Motostoke's lower Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-x-speed\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"X Speed\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon during battle, this item will raise the Speed of the Pokémon by 2 stages.\\nMain way to obtain: Buy in Hammerlocke's central Pokémon Center\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-yache-berry\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Yache Berry\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If a Pokémon holds one, it can eat this Berry to halve the damage taken from one supereffective Ice-type move.\\nMain way to obtain: Collect from the Berry tree at the Lake of Outrage in the Wild Area\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-zinc\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Zinc\",\"body\":\"Description: A consumable item. If used on a Pokémon, thi"
"s item will add base points to the Pokémon's Sp. Def stat.\\nMain way to obtain: Get at Hammerlocke's BP Shop\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"items-zoom-lens\",\"category\":\"Items\",\"title\":\"Zoom Lens\",\"body\":\"Description: A nonconsumable item. If held by a Pokémon, this item will boost the holder's accuracy by 20% if its targets have already moved that turn.\\nMain way to obtain: Find on Route 9 (Circhester Bay)\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 370–380\"},{\"key\":\"league-cards-card-maker-workflow-and-album\",\"category\":\"League Cards\",\"title\":\"Card Maker workflow and album\",\"body\":\"Use Card Maker at Rotomi. Choose background, effects and frame, then set expression, pose, position, angle and zoom; choose a coating before printing. Update the card after changing your appearance if you want its portrait refreshed. Card backgrounds and the five other Card categories list individual unlock-group members; the source uses visual choices without stable descr"
"iptive names for many poses and expressions, so group-relative variants are used here. The local guide tracks NPC League Card ownership separately from Card Maker availability. Compatible Let’s Go and Pokémon Quest records are separate unlocks.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 301–312\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-airstream\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Airstream\",\"body\":\"Type: Flying\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Flying-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Raises the user's and ally Pokémon's Speed by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-darkness\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Darkness\",\"body\":\"Type: Dark\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Dark-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dy"
"namax Pokémon. Lowers opposing Pokémon's Sp. Def by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-flare\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Flare\",\"body\":\"Type: Fire\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Fire-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Changes the weather condition to harsh sunlight for 5 turns, boosting the power of Fire-type moves by 50% and reducing the power of Water-type moves by 50%.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-flutterby\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Flutterby\",\"body\":\"Type: Bug\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Bug-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon"
". Lowers opposing Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-geyser\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Geyser\",\"body\":\"Type: Water\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Water-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Changes the weather condition to rain for 5 turns, boosting the power of Water-type moves by 50% and reducing the power of Fire-type moves by 50%.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-guard\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Guard\",\"body\":\"Type: Normal\\nCategory: Status\\nTargets: Self\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any status move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. The user protects itself from all moves used on the sa"
"me turn. This move becomes more likely to fail if used repeatedly.\\nTarget pattern: The user.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-hailstorm\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Hailstorm\",\"body\":\"Type: Ice\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Ice-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Changes the weather condition to hail for 5 turns. All Pokémon other than Ice types take damage at the end of each turn equal to 1/16 of their max HP.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-knuckle\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Knuckle\",\"body\":\"Type: Fighting\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Fighting-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Raises the user's and ally Pokémon's Attack "
"by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-lightning\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Lightning\",\"body\":\"Type: Electric\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Electric-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Electrifies the battlefield for 5 turns. During that time, Pokémon on the ground will be able to do 50% more damage with Electric-type moves and cannot fall asleep.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-mindstorm\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Mindstorm\",\"body\":\"Type: Psychic\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Psychic-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Covers the batt"
"lefield with psychic energy for 5 turns. During that time, Pokémon on the ground will be able to do 50% more damage with Psychic-type moves and will evade high-priority moves.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-ooze\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Ooze\",\"body\":\"Type: Poison\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Poison-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Raises the user's and ally Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-overgrowth\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Overgrowth\",\"body\":\"Type: Grass\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Grass-type move will turn into this move when us"
"ed by a Dynamax Pokémon. Covers the battlefield with grass for 5 turns. During that time, Pokémon on the ground will be able to do 50% more damage with Grass-type moves and will recover 1/16 of their max HP at the end of each turn. Damage done to Pokémon on the ground by Bulldoze or Earthquake is also halved during this time.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-phantasm\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Phantasm\",\"body\":\"Type: Ghost\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Ghost-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Lowers opposing Pokémon's Defense by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-quake\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Quake\",\"body\":\"Type: Ground"
"\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Ground-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Raises the user's and ally Pokémon's Sp. Def by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-rockfall\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Rockfall\",\"body\":\"Type: Rock\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Rock-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Changes the weather condition to sandstorm for 5 turns, boosting the Sp. Def of Rock-type Pokémon by 50%. All Pokémon other than Ground, Rock, and Steel types take damage at the end of each turn equal to 1/16 of their max HP.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max"
"-starfall\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Starfall\",\"body\":\"Type: Fairy\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Fairy-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Covers the battlefield with mist for 5 turns. During that time, Pokémon on the ground cannot be afflicted with new status conditions or confusion. Damage done to Pokémon on the ground by Dragon-type moves is also halved during this time.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-steelspike\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Steelspike\",\"body\":\"Type: Steel\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Steel-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Raises the user's and ally Pokémon's Defense by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in mul"
"ti-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-strike\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Strike\",\"body\":\"Type: Normal\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Normal-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Lowers opposing Pokémon's Speed by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"max-moves-max-wyrmwind\",\"category\":\"Max moves\",\"title\":\"Max Wyrmwind\",\"body\":\"Type: Dragon\\nCategory: Physical or Special\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nEffect: Any damage-dealing Dragon-type move will turn into this move when used by a Dynamax Pokémon. Lowers opposing Pokémon's Attack by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 353\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-0\",\"category\":"
"\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority +0\",\"body\":\"All moves that are not listed here have standard priority.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-1\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority +1\",\"body\":\"Aqua Jet, Baby-Doll Eyes, Bullet Punch, Ice Shard, Mach Punch, Quick Attack, Shadow Sneak, Sucker Punch, Vacuum Wave, Water Shuriken.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-2\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority +2\",\"body\":\"Ally Switch, Extreme Speed, Feint, First Impression, Follow Me, Rage Powder.\\nHighe"
"r priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-3\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority +3\",\"body\":\"Crafty Shield, Fake Out, Quick Guard, Wide Guard.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-4\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority +4\",\"body\":\"Baneful Bunker, Detect, Endure, King's Shield, Magic Coat, Max Guard, Obstruct, Protect, Spiky Shield.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter t"
"hese rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-5\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority +5\",\"body\":\"Helping Hand.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-1-2\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority -1\",\"body\":\"Vital Throw.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-3-2\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority -3\",\"body\":\"Focus Punch, Shell Trap.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed o"
"rdering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-4-2\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority -4\",\"body\":\"Avalanche, Revenge.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-5-2\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority -5\",\"body\":\"Counter, Mirror Coat.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-6\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority -6\",\"body\":\"Circle Throw, Dragon Tail, Roar, Telepo"
"rt, Whirlwind.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"move-priority-priority-7\",\"category\":\"Move priority\",\"title\":\"Priority -7\",\"body\":\"Trick Room.\\nHigher priority acts first; within a bracket, Speed normally decides. Trick Room reverses the Speed ordering, not priority brackets. Abilities and special effects can alter these rules.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 181–183, 352\"},{\"key\":\"moves-absorb\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Absorb\",\"body\":\"Type: Grass\\nCategory: Special\\nPower: 20\\nAccuracy: 100\\nPP: 25\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: 90\\nEffect: Restores the user's HP by an amount equal to 1/2 of the damage dealt to the target.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\\nPP is the base maximum bef"
"ore PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-acid\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Acid\",\"body\":\"Type: Poison\\nCategory: Special\\nPower: 40\\nAccuracy: 100\\nPP: 30\\nTargets: Many Others\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: 70\\nEffect: Has a 10% chance of lowering the targets' Sp. Def by 1 stage.\\nTarget pattern: Both opponents in Doubles; the single opponent in Singles or a raid.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-acid-armor\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Acid Armor\",\"body\":\"Type: Poison\\nCategory: Status\\nPower: —\\nAccuracy: —\\nPP: 20\\nTargets: Self\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: —\\nEffect: Raises the user's Defense by 2 stages.\\nTarget pattern: The"
" user.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-acid-spray\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Acid Spray\",\"body\":\"Type: Poison\\nCategory: Special\\nPower: 40\\nAccuracy: 100\\nPP: 20\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: 70\\nEffect: Lowers the target's Sp. Def by 2 stages.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-acrobatics\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Acrobatics\",\"body\":\"Type: Flying\\nCategory: Physical\\nPower: 55\\nAccuracy: 100\\nPP: 15\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: Yes\\nMax Move power: 110\\nEffect: This move's power is doubled i"
"f the user isn't holding an item.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-acupressure\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Acupressure\",\"body\":\"Type: Normal\\nCategory: Status\\nPower: —\\nAccuracy: —\\nPP: 30\\nTargets: Self/Ally\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: —\\nEffect: Raises a random stat by 2 stages. Stats that were already boosted to the max will not be selected.\\nTarget pattern: The user or an ally.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-aerial-ace\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Aerial Ace\",\"body\":\"Type: Flying\\nCategory: Physical\\nP"
"ower: 60\\nAccuracy: —\\nPP: 20\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: Yes\\nMax Move power: 110\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\\nNo additional effect is listed in the printed move table.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-after-you\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"After You\",\"body\":\"Type: Normal\\nCategory: Status\\nPower: —\\nAccuracy: —\\nPP: 15\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: —\\nEffect: Forces the target to use its move immediately after this move is used, regardless of the target's Speed. This move fails if the user doesn't act before the target or if the target was going to use its move right after anyway.\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accurac"
"y is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-agility\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Agility\",\"body\":\"Type: Psychic\\nCategory: Status\\nPower: —\\nAccuracy: —\\nPP: 30\\nTargets: Self\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: —\\nEffect: Raises the user's Speed by 2 stages.\\nTarget pattern: The user.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-air-cutter\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Air Cutter\",\"body\":\"Type: Flying\\nCategory: Special\\nPower: 60\\nAccuracy: 95\\nPP: 25\\nTargets: Many Others\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: 110\\nEffect: This move is more likely than average to deliver a critical hit.\\nTarget pattern: Both opponents in Doubles; the single opponent in Singles or a raid.\\nPP is the "
"base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-air-slash\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Air Slash\",\"body\":\"Type: Flying\\nCategory: Special\\nPower: 75\\nAccuracy: 95\\nPP: 15\\nTargets: Normal\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: 130\\nEffect: Has a 30% chance of making the target flinch (unable to use moves on that turn).\\nTarget pattern: One selected target; allies can be chosen in multi-Pokémon battles.\\nPP is the base maximum before PP Up effects. Accuracy is a percentage; “—” means no ordinary accuracy check, although other conditions can still block the move.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 336–351\"},{\"key\":\"moves-ally-switch\",\"category\":\"Moves\",\"title\":\"Ally Switch\",\"body\":\"Type: Psychic\\nCategory: Status\\nPower: —\\nAccuracy: —\\nPP: 15\\nTargets: Self\\nContact: No\\nMax Move power: —\\nEffect: A high-priority m"
