"ey\":\"nursery-incense-bonsly\",\"category\":\"Nursery incense\",\"title\":\"Bonsly\",\"body\":\"Parent family: Sudowoodo.\\nRequired held item: Rock Incense. The appropriate parent must hold it while breeding to obtain Bonsly; without it, the Egg skips that baby stage. Use a compatible partner or Ditto.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 234–240\"},{\"key\":\"nursery-incense-budew\",\"category\":\"Nursery incense\",\"title\":\"Budew\",\"body\":\"Parent family: Roselia or Roserade.\\nRequired held item: Rose Incense. The appropriate parent must hold it while breeding to obtain Budew; without it, the Egg skips that baby stage. Use a compatible partner or Ditto.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 234–240\"},{\"key\":\"nursery-incense-mantyke\",\"category\":\"Nursery incense\",\"title\":\"Mantyke\",\"body\":\"Parent family: Mantine.\\nRequired held item: Wave Incense. The appropriate parent must hold it while breeding to obtain Mantyke; without it, the Egg skips that baby stage. Use a compatible partner or Ditto.\","
"\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 234–240\"},{\"key\":\"nursery-incense-mime-jr\",\"category\":\"Nursery incense\",\"title\":\"Mime Jr.\",\"body\":\"Parent family: Mr. Mime or Mr. Rime.\\nRequired held item: Odd Incense. The appropriate parent must hold it while breeding to obtain Mime Jr.; without it, the Egg skips that baby stage. Use a compatible partner or Ditto.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 234–240\"},{\"key\":\"nursery-incense-munchlax\",\"category\":\"Nursery incense\",\"title\":\"Munchlax\",\"body\":\"Parent family: Snorlax.\\nRequired held item: Full Incense. The appropriate parent must hold it while breeding to obtain Munchlax; without it, the Egg skips that baby stage. Use a compatible partner or Ditto.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 234–240\"},{\"key\":\"nursery-incense-wynaut\",\"category\":\"Nursery incense\",\"title\":\"Wynaut\",\"body\":\"Parent family: Wobbuffet.\\nRequired held item: Lax Incense. The appropriate parent must hold it while breeding to obtain Wynaut; without it,"
" the Egg skips that baby stage. Use a compatible partner or Ditto.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 234–240\"},{\"key\":\"nursery-mechanics-inherited-ivs-nature-ability-and-moves\",\"category\":\"Nursery mechanics\",\"title\":\"Inherited IVs, Nature, Ability and moves\",\"body\":\"An Egg normally inherits three IVs chosen from the parents. A Destiny Knot held by either parent makes that five; a Power item guarantees the corresponding stat from its holder. Everstone passes its holder’s Nature and can preserve the appropriate regional form. Hidden Ability inheritance depends on the parent’s Ability and pairing; an Ability Capsule does not create a Hidden Ability. Compatible Egg Moves can be inherited. In these games, two Pokémon of the same species can also transfer an Egg Move at the Nursery when the recipient has an empty move slot; sex does not matter for this move transfer.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 237–240\"},{\"key\":\"nursery-mechanics-pairing-eggs-and-hatching\",\"cate"
"gory\":\"Nursery mechanics\",\"title\":\"Pairing, Eggs and hatching\",\"body\":\"Leave two compatible Pokémon at either Nursery: Route 5 or Bridge Field. Opposite sexes need a shared Egg Group; a breedable species can pair with Ditto regardless of sex. Undiscovered-group Pokémon and two Ditto do not produce Eggs. The offspring normally belongs to the female parent’s evolutionary family, or the non-Ditto parent’s family when Ditto is used. Different original Trainers improve Egg generation odds; the Oval Charm helps. Pay to collect an Egg, keep it in your party and travel to hatch it. Flame Body or Steam Engine speeds hatching. Nursery deposits do not gain experience here.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 234–237\"},{\"key\":\"nursery-mechanics-pok-ball-and-special-family-inheritance\",\"category\":\"Nursery mechanics\",\"title\":\"Poké Ball and special-family inheritance\",\"body\":\"Eggs can inherit a parent’s Poké Ball, but Master Balls and Cherish Balls do not pass down. Same-species parents can"
" pass either eligible parent’s ball; when paired with Ditto, the non-Ditto parent supplies the ball. Ditto does not supply a ball, moves or species. Nidoran and Volbeat/Illumise families have special offspring rules; check species availability rather than assuming every transferred Pokémon is part of the 400-entry base Galar Dex. Incense is required for the baby species listed in Nursery incense.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 238–240\"},{\"key\":\"pickup-balm-mushroom\",\"category\":\"Pickup\",\"title\":\"Balm Mushroom\",\"body\":\"Relative reward frequency by level band, from lowest to highest:\\nLevel 1–10: Not in this band\\nLevel 11–20: Not in this band\\nLevel 21–30: Very rare\\nLevel 31–40: Rare\\nLevel 41–50: Rare\\nLevel 51–60: Rare\\nLevel 61–70: Rare\\nLevel 71–80: Rare\\nLevel 81–90: Rare\\nLevel 91–100: Rare\\nA party Pokémon needs Pickup and an empty held-item slot. Check its held item after battles. The printed table gives relative rarity, not exact probabilities.\",\"citation\":\"Offic"
"ial Sword/Shield guide, pp. 364; level-band labels checked against https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pickup\"},{\"key\":\"pickup-big-mushroom\",\"category\":\"Pickup\",\"title\":\"Big Mushroom\",\"body\":\"Relative reward frequency by level band, from lowest to highest:\\nLevel 1–10: Rare\\nLevel 11–20: Uncommon\\nLevel 21–30: Uncommon\\nLevel 31–40: Not in this band\\nLevel 41–50: Not in this band\\nLevel 51–60: Not in this band\\nLevel 61–70: Not in this band\\nLevel 71–80: Not in this band\\nLevel 81–90: Not in this band\\nLevel 91–100: Not in this band\\nA party Pokémon needs Pickup and an empty held-item slot. Check its held item after battles. The printed table gives relative rarity, not exact probabilities.\",\"citation\":\"Official Sword/Shield guide, pp. 364; level-band labels checked against https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pickup\"},{\"key\":\"pickup-big-nugget\",\"category\":\"Pickup\",\"title\":\"Big Nugget\",\"body\":\"Relative reward frequency by level band, from lowest to highest:\\nLevel 1–10: Not in th"
